var e=[{id:`exam-001`,code:`B1-001`,name:`Đề thi thử số 1`,type:`basic`,level:`B1`,difficulty:`easy`,durationMin:60,description:`Đề thi thử số 1 mức cơ bản với các tình huống quen thuộc trong đời sống hằng ngày. Phù hợp cho người học làm quen với cấu trúc đề và cách chấm điểm tự động.`,sections:[{id:`listening`,skill:`listening`,title:`Listening`,durationMin:30,transcript:`A: Good afternoon. I'd like to book a room for tonight, please.(B: We have a single room available for ninety pounds a night.(A: Actually, I need a double room for two nights.(B: In that case, that will be two hundred pounds altogether.(A: Excuse me, I'd like to borrow this book. Is it still available?(B: Yes, but you must bring it back by Friday next week.(A: Friday? That's the day after tomorrow.(B: Yes, but you can renew it online if you need more time.(A: How do I get to the city museum from here?(B: Take the number 12 bus and get off at the market square.(A: Is it far from the bus stop?(B: No, it's only a two-minute walk behind the old church.(A: Hello, I'd like to make an appointment with Dr. Smith.(B: He's fully booked on Monday, but he's free on Thursday at four o'clock.(A: Thursday afternoon suits me perfectly.(B: Good. Please arrive ten minutes early to fill in a form.(A: How much is a ticket for Saturday's concert?(B: They're thirty pounds each, but students get a twenty-percent discount.(A: I'm a student, so I'll take one, please.(B: That'll be twenty-four pounds, then.(Speaker: Welcome to the information point of the Green Town festival.(Speaker: The festival takes place this Saturday and Sunday in Riverside Park.(Speaker: There will be live music, a food market, and activities for children.(Speaker: Entry is free, but you need a wristband for the evening concerts.(Speaker: Wristbands can be collected at the main gate from ten in the morning until four in the afternoon.(Speaker: Please bring a water bottle, because there are very few shops inside the park.(Speaker: If it rains, the food market will move into the community hall next to the gate.(Speaker: Good morning. Here is the news about the Central Library.(Speaker: From next month, the library will stay open until eight o'clock on weekdays.(Speaker: Saturday hours stay the same, from nine to five.(Speaker: The reading room on the first floor is now open to everyone, not only to members.(Speaker: However, you still need a library card if you want to borrow books.(Speaker: Members can borrow up to eight books at a time and keep them for three weeks.(Speaker: Children under twelve must be accompanied by an adult.(Speaker: Finally, the cafe on the ground floor will close earlier, at six o'clock.`.split(`(`),questions:[{id:1,type:`multiple_choice`,question:`Part 1. Conversation 1. What does the customer want to book?`,options:[`A single room for one night`,`A double room for one night`,`A double room for two nights`,`A single room for two nights`],answer:2,transcriptRef:2,explanationVi:`transcriptRef = 2, người nói A xác nhận: 'Actually, I need a double room for two nights' → đáp án C. A và D sai vì loại phòng không đúng; B sai vì thiếu số đêm (khách đổi từ 1 đêm lên 2 đêm ở dòng 2).`},{id:2,type:`multiple_choice`,question:`Part 1. Conversation 2. When must the book be returned?`,options:[`By Friday next week`,`By Friday this week`,`By Wednesday this week`,`By Sunday next week`],answer:0,transcriptRef:5,explanationVi:`transcriptRef = 5: 'you must bring it back by Friday next week' → đáp án A. B và C sai vì nhầm tuần (this week); D không được nhắc tới — dòng 6 chỉ nói thứ Sáu là ngày kia, không phải hạn cuối.`},{id:3,type:`multiple_choice`,question:`Part 1. Conversation 3. How will the visitor get to the city museum?`,options:[`By taxi`,`By the number 12 bus`,`On foot for about ten minutes`,`By the number 21 bus`],answer:1,transcriptRef:9,explanationVi:`transcriptRef = 9: 'Take the number 12 bus and get off at the market square' → đáp án B. C sai vì chỉ đi bộ 2 phút từ trạm buýt đến bảo tàng (dòng 11); A và D hoàn toàn không được nhắc trong hội thoại.`},{id:4,type:`multiple_choice`,question:`Part 1. Conversation 4. When is the appointment with Dr. Smith?`,options:[`Thursday at four o'clock`,`Thursday at two o'clock`,`Friday at four o'clock`,`Monday at four o'clock`],answer:0,transcriptRef:13,explanationVi:`transcriptRef = 13: bác sĩ 'free on Thursday at four o'clock' → đáp án A. D sai vì thứ Hai đã kín lịch (fully booked); B và C sai ở giờ hoặc ngày, không khớp mốc giờ nào trong đoạn.`},{id:5,type:`multiple_choice`,question:`Part 1. Conversation 5. How much will the student pay for the concert ticket?`,options:[`£30`,`£36`,`£24`,`£27`],answer:2,transcriptRef:19,explanationVi:`Vé £30 và sinh viên được giảm 20% (dòng 17): 30 − 6 = £24, dòng 19 xác nhận 'That'll be twenty-four pounds' → đáp án C. A là giá gốc chưa giảm; B là tăng 20%; D là giảm 10%.`},{id:6,type:`multiple_choice`,question:`Part 2. Talk 1. What is the speaker mainly doing?`,options:[`Reviewing a local restaurant`,`Giving information about a festival`,`Selling concert tickets`,`Reporting the weather forecast`],answer:1,transcriptRef:20,explanationVi:`transcriptRef = 20–22 mở đầu bằng 'information point' và liệt kê hoạt động của lễ hội → người nói đang cung cấp thông tin (B). C sai vì vé vào cửa miễn phí (dòng 23); A và D không liên quan nội dung đoạn.`},{id:7,type:`multiple_choice`,question:`Part 2. Talk 1. What does the speaker ask listeners to bring?`,options:[`A wristband`,`A shopping bag`,`A water bottle`,`A raincoat`],answer:2,transcriptRef:25,explanationVi:`transcriptRef = 25: 'Please bring a water bottle, because there are very few shops inside the park' → đáp án C. A sai vì vòng tay (wristband) phải tự đến cổng lấy (dòng 24), không phải mang theo; B và D không được nhắc tới.`},{id:8,type:`multiple_choice`,question:`Part 2. Talk 2. What is the library's new closing time on weekdays?`,options:[`Eight o'clock`,`Six o'clock`,`Five o'clock`,`Nine o'clock`],answer:0,transcriptRef:28,explanationVi:`transcriptRef = 28: 'the library will stay open until eight o'clock on weekdays' → đáp án A. B là giờ đóng cửa của quán cafe (dòng 34); C là giờ đóng cửa thứ Bảy (dòng 29); D là giờ mở cửa thứ Bảy.`},{id:9,type:`multiple_choice`,question:`Part 2. Talk 2. What do you need in order to borrow books?`,options:[`An adult`,`A wristband`,`A reading-room pass`,`A library card`],answer:3,transcriptRef:31,explanationVi:`transcriptRef = 31: 'you still need a library card if you want to borrow books' → đáp án D. B chỉ áp dụng cho trẻ dưới 12 tuổi khi đến thư viện (dòng 33); A và C không được nhắc; phòng đọc thứ nhất thì mở cho tất cả nên không cần thẻ để vào đọc.`},{id:10,type:`multiple_choice`,question:`Part 2. Talk 2. Who can use the first-floor reading room now?`,options:[`Only library members`,`Everyone`,`Children under twelve`,`Teachers only`],answer:1,transcriptRef:30,explanationVi:`transcriptRef = 30: phòng đọc 'now open to everyone, not only to members' → đáp án B. A trái ngược với 'not only to members'; C bị giới hạn sai (trẻ em vẫn cần người lớn đi kèm nhưng không bị cấm); D không được nhắc tới.`}]},{id:`reading`,skill:`reading`,title:`Reading`,durationMin:30,paragraphs:[`Many parents worry that teenagers who never enter the kitchen will struggle when they leave home. However, schools that offer cooking classes report that their students eat more vegetables and feel more confident. A recent survey of two hundred students found that those who cooked at least twice a week were also better at planning their weekly spending. Experts say that cooking is not only a practical skill but also a way for families to spend time together without screens.`,`Every summer, cities across Europe fill their streets with cyclists, but getting people to cycle in winter remains a challenge. The northern city of Aarhus solved part of the problem by building covered bike lanes that are cleaned of ice every morning. Since the lanes opened, the number of winter cyclists has risen by thirty percent. Shop owners in the centre say that customers arrive more often and stay longer, because parking a bicycle is easier than finding a space for a car. The city now plans to extend the network to the suburbs.`,`Students who stay up late often believe that they can catch up on sleep at the weekend. Researchers disagree. In an experiment with eighty teenagers, those who kept a regular bedtime scored higher in morning tests than those who slept late on Saturday and Sunday. The researchers explain that the brain needs a steady rhythm, not a large amount of sleep after a long week. They recommend keeping the same waking time every day, even during holidays, and avoiding bright screens for an hour before bed.`,`When a group of residents in Manchester found an empty lot behind their flats, they asked the council for permission to turn it into a garden. Today the half-hectare plot produces tomatoes, herbs, and apples for about forty families. The garden is run by volunteers, and new members are shown how to use the tools before they work alone. Older residents say that the garden has given them a reason to go outside every day, while children enjoy collecting eggs from the small hen house.`],questions:[{id:11,type:`multiple_choice`,question:`According to the survey, students who cooked at least twice a week were better at something. What was it?`,options:[`Planning their weekly spending`,`Growing vegetables at school`,`Reading recipes aloud`,`Writing school reports`],answer:0,paragraphRef:0,locationVi:`Đoạn 1, câu 'A recent survey ... were also better at planning their weekly spending.'`,explanationVi:`Câu khảo sát nêu rõ nhóm nấu ăn ≥2 lần/tuần 'were also better at planning their weekly spending' → A đúng. B, C, D là các hoạt động hoàn toàn không xuất hiện trong đoạn 1.`},{id:12,type:`multiple_choice`,question:`What do schools with cooking classes report about their students?`,options:[`They sleep better at night.`,`They spend more time outdoors.`,`They eat more vegetables and feel more confident.`,`They get higher marks in science.`],answer:2,paragraphRef:0,locationVi:`Đoạn 1, câu 'However, schools that offer cooking classes report that their students eat more vegetables and feel more confident.'`,explanationVi:`Đoạn 1 nói đúng là 'eat more vegetables and feel more confident' → C đúng. A, B, D không phải điều trường học báo cáo trong đoạn; chúng chỉ là những kết quả plausible nhưng không có bằng chứng.`},{id:13,type:`true_false_not_given`,question:`Statement: The survey mentioned in the text included students from five different countries.`,options:[`True`,`False`,`Not Given`],answer:2,paragraphRef:0,locationVi:`Đoạn 1, câu 'A recent survey of two hundred students ...'`,explanationVi:`Đoạn chỉ nói khảo sát gồm hai trăm học sinh, hoàn toàn không đề cập số quốc gia hay địa điểm → Not Given. Không đủ thông tin để kết luận đúng hay sai.`},{id:14,type:`gap_filling`,question:`Complete the sentence using NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage. According to experts, cooking gives families a chance to spend time together without ___.`,answer:`screens`,paragraphRef:0,locationVi:`Đoạn 1, câu cuối '... a way for families to spend time together without screens.'`,explanationVi:`Câu cuối đoạn 1 kết thúc bằng 'without screens' → điền 'screens'. Các từ khác như 'money' hay 'teachers' không nằm trong câu gốc nên sai.`},{id:15,type:`multiple_choice`,question:`What is the main idea of the first paragraph?`,options:[`Parents should cook for their children every day.`,`Ready meals are cheaper than home cooking.`,`Schools should teach more science.`,`Cooking classes bring practical and social benefits to students and families.`],answer:3,paragraphRef:0,locationVi:`Đoạn 1 (toàn đoạn), đặc biệt câu 2 và câu cuối.`,explanationVi:`Đoạn nêu nhiều lợi ích của lớp nấu ăn (ăn nhiều rau, tự tin, quản lý chi tiêu, gắn kết gia đình) → D đúng. A, B, C chỉ là quá trình suy luận thêm hoặc chủ đề không được nói tới trong đoạn.`},{id:16,type:`multiple_choice`,question:`How did the city of Aarhus reduce the problem of winter cycling?`,options:[`By giving free bicycles to residents.`,`By building covered bike lanes cleaned of ice every morning.`,`By banning cars from the centre.`,`By making bus travel cheaper.`],answer:1,paragraphRef:1,locationVi:`Đoạn 2, câu 'The northern city of Aarhus solved part of the problem by building covered bike lanes that are cleaned of ice every morning.'`,explanationVi:`Câu thứ 2 của đoạn 2 nêu đúng giải pháp 'covered bike lanes ... cleaned of ice every morning' → B đúng. A, C, D là các biện pháp không hề được nhắc đến.`},{id:17,type:`multiple_choice`,question:`According to shop owners, what has happened since the lanes opened?`,options:[`Customers arrive less often and leave earlier.`,`Customers prefer to shop online in winter.`,`Customers arrive more often and stay longer.`,`Customers complain about the noise of cyclists.`],answer:2,paragraphRef:1,locationVi:`Đoạn 2, câu 'Shop owners in the centre say that customers arrive more often and stay longer ...'`,explanationVi:`Câu về chủ cửa hàng nói khách 'arrive more often and stay longer' → C đúng. A trái ngược với nội dung đoạn; B và D không được nêu trong đoạn.`},{id:18,type:`true_false_not_given`,question:`Statement: The number of winter cyclists in Aarhus has risen by about thirty percent.`,options:[`True`,`False`,`Not Given`],answer:0,paragraphRef:1,locationVi:`Đoạn 2, câu 'Since the lanes opened, the number of winter cyclists has risen by thirty percent.'`,explanationVi:`Câu thứ 3 của đoạn 2 nêu đúng 'risen by thirty percent' → True. Đoạn không có thông tin nào mâu thuẫn với con số này.`},{id:19,type:`gap_filling`,question:`Complete the sentence using NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage. The covered bike ___ are cleaned of ice every morning.`,answer:`lanes`,paragraphRef:1,locationVi:`Đoạn 2, câu '... by building covered bike lanes that are cleaned of ice every morning.'`,explanationVi:`Câu 'The covered bike ___ are cleaned' cần danh từ số nhiều → 'lanes' (từ vựng đúng trong đoạn 2). 'Lane' (số ít) sai ngữ pháp với 'are'; các từ khác không xuất hiện trong đoạn.`},{id:20,type:`multiple_choice`,question:`What does the writer say remains a challenge?`,options:[`Getting people to cycle in winter.`,`Filling the streets with cyclists in summer.`,`Finding parking spaces for cars.`,`Building shops in the city centre.`],answer:0,paragraphRef:1,locationVi:`Đoạn 2, câu đầu '... but getting people to cycle in winter remains a challenge.'`,explanationVi:`Câu mở đầu đoạn 2 nêu rõ 'getting people to cycle in winter remains a challenge' → A đúng. B là điều đang diễn ra tốt (không phải thách thức); C, D không được nhắc tới.`},{id:21,type:`multiple_choice`,question:`In the experiment, what happened to the teenagers who kept a regular bedtime?`,options:[`They slept later on Saturday and Sunday.`,`They scored higher in morning tests.`,`They avoided bright screens before bed.`,`They took the same tests in the afternoon.`],answer:1,paragraphRef:2,locationVi:`Đoạn 3, câu 'In an experiment with eighty teenagers, those who kept a regular bedtime scored higher in morning tests ...'`,explanationVi:`Nhóm giữ giờ ngủ đều 'scored higher in morning tests' → B đúng. A mô tả nhóm đối lập (ngủ cuối tuần); C là lời khuyên ở câu cuối, không phải kết quả thí nghiệm; D không được nhắc.`},{id:22,type:`multiple_choice`,question:`What do the researchers' results suggest?`,options:[`The brain needs a large amount of sleep after a long week.`,`Weekend sleep can replace weekday sleep.`,`Morning tests are not a fair measure.`,`A steady rhythm matters more than the total amount of sleep.`],answer:3,paragraphRef:2,locationVi:`Đoạn 3, câu 'The researchers explain that the brain needs a steady rhythm, not a large amount of sleep after a long week.'`,explanationVi:`Các nhà nghiên cứu khẳng định 'needs a steady rhythm, not a large amount of sleep' → D đúng. A và B trái ngược với quan điểm này; C không được thảo luận trong đoạn.`},{id:23,type:`true_false_not_given`,question:`Statement: Researchers suggest that students should sleep later during the holidays.`,options:[`True`,`False`,`Not Given`],answer:1,paragraphRef:2,locationVi:`Đoạn 3, câu cuối 'They recommend keeping the same waking time every day, even during holidays ...'`,explanationVi:`Lời khuyên là giữ giờ thức dậy như nhau 'even during holidays' → ngủ dậy muộn hơn vào kỳ nghỉ trái với khuyến nghị này → False.`},{id:24,type:`gap_filling`,question:`Complete the sentence using NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage. Researchers recommend keeping the same waking ___ every day, even during holidays.`,answer:`time`,paragraphRef:2,locationVi:`Đoạn 3, câu cuối 'They recommend keeping the same waking time every day ...'`,explanationVi:`Câu gốc là 'keeping the same waking time' → điền 'time'. 'Hour' hay 'schedule' không nằm trong câu gốc nên không phải đáp án theo yêu cầu 'from the passage'.`},{id:25,type:`multiple_choice`,question:`What do the researchers recommend?`,options:[`Sleeping as much as possible at the weekend.`,`Going to bed one hour earlier every night.`,`Keeping a consistent waking time and avoiding screens before bed.`,`Taking morning tests only on weekdays.`],answer:2,paragraphRef:2,locationVi:`Đoạn 3, câu cuối 'They recommend keeping the same waking time ... and avoiding bright screens for an hour before bed.'`,explanationVi:`Lời khuyên gồm hai việc: giờ thức dậy cố định + tránh màn hình sáng trước khi ngủ → C đúng. A ngược với kết luận của đoạn; B và D không được nêu.`},{id:26,type:`multiple_choice`,question:`How did the community garden project begin?`,options:[`Residents asked the council for permission to use an empty lot.`,`The council built a garden behind the flats.`,`A local company donated the land.`,`Children collected eggs and planted trees.`],answer:0,paragraphRef:3,locationVi:`Đoạn 4, câu đầu 'When a group of residents ... asked the council for permission to turn it into a garden.'`,explanationVi:`Câu mở đầu cho thấy người dân tự đề xuất và xin phép hội đồng → A đúng. B sai vì hội đồng không tự xây; C, D không được nhắc trong đoạn.`},{id:27,type:`multiple_choice`,question:`What do older residents say about the garden?`,options:[`It gives them free vegetables all year.`,`It gives them a reason to go outside every day.`,`It is too much work for them.`,`It has replaced their supermarket.`],answer:1,paragraphRef:3,locationVi:`Đoạn 4, câu 'Older residents say that the garden has given them a reason to go outside every day ...'`,explanationVi:`Câu về người cao tuổi nói garden 'gave them a reason to go outside every day' → B đúng. A, D phóng to sai (đoạn không nói thay thế siêu thị hay miễn phí quanh năm); C trái với tinh thần tích cực của đoạn.`},{id:28,type:`true_false_not_given`,question:`Statement: New members are not allowed to use the tools alone at first.`,options:[`True`,`False`,`Not Given`],answer:0,paragraphRef:3,locationVi:`Đoạn 4, câu '... new members are shown how to use the tools before they work alone.'`,explanationVi:`Câu này nói thành viên mới được hướng dẫn dùng dụng cụ 'before they work alone' → trước đó họ không làm việc một mình → Statement True.`},{id:29,type:`gap_filling`,question:`Complete the sentence using NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage. The garden is run by a group of ___ who give their time freely.`,answer:`volunteers`,paragraphRef:3,locationVi:`Đoạn 4, câu 'The garden is run by volunteers ...'`,explanationVi:`Câu gốc là 'The garden is run by volunteers'; cụm 'a group of ___' yêu cầu danh từ số nhiều → 'volunteers'. 'Workers' hay 'residents' không phải từ dùng trong câu gốc.`},{id:30,type:`multiple_choice`,question:`What do children enjoy collecting from the small hen house?`,options:[`Herbs.`,`Apples.`,`Tomatoes.`,`Eggs.`],answer:3,paragraphRef:3,locationVi:`Đoạn 4, câu cuối '... children enjoy collecting eggs from the small hen house.'`,explanationVi:`Câu cuối đoạn 4 nêu trẻ em hái 'eggs' từ chuồng gà nhỏ → D đúng. A, B, C là sản phẩm của khu vườn nhưng không phải thứ trẻ em nhặt từ chuồng gà.`}]},{id:`writing`,skill:`writing`,title:`Writing`,promptVi:`Viết một đoạn văn ngắn (80–120 từ) nêu quan điểm của em về việc giới trẻ nên tự nấu ăn ở nhà. Đưa ra ít nhất hai lý do và một ví dụ cụ thể.`,requirementsVi:[`Đúng số từ: 80–120 từ`,`Nêu rõ quan điểm ở câu đầu tiên`,`Đưa ít nhất hai lý do để ủng hộ quan điểm`,`Kèm ít nhất một ví dụ cụ thể từ cuộc sống`,`Dùng từ nối (ví dụ: first, second, however, because, for example)`],minWords:80,maxWords:120,sampleAnswer:`In my opinion, young people should learn to cook simple meals at home. First, cooking is a life skill: students who leave for university or work will not always be able to buy ready meals. Second, cooking helps families spend time together. In my family, my brother and I cook one dinner a week, and we talk about our day while we prepare the food. Of course, cooking takes time, but the dishes are usually healthier and cheaper than takeaway food. For this reason, I believe that schools could also offer short cooking classes.`},{id:`speaking`,skill:`speaking`,title:`Speaking`,promptVi:`Nói trong 2 phút về một kỹ năng mà em đã học ngoài trường học. Hãy giải thích: em đã học kỹ năng đó như thế nào, em thường dùng nó ở đâu, và vì sao nó hữu ích.`,timeLimitSec:120,sampleAnswer:`Two years ago, I learned how to fix a flat bicycle tyre, and it has become one of the most useful skills I have. My father showed me the first time, and then I practised alone. The process is simple: you remove the wheel, find the hole, dry it, and glue a small patch over it. I use this skill almost every week because I cycle to school. Last month, my friend had a flat tyre near the city market, and I repaired it in ten minutes. Because of that, we did not have to push the bike home. I think practical skills like this save time and money, and they also make you more confident.`}]},{id:`exam-002`,code:`B1-002`,name:`Đề thi thử số 2`,type:`intermediate`,level:`B1`,difficulty:`medium`,durationMin:60,description:`Đề thi thử số 2 mức trung bình với chủ đề đa dạng hơn và các bẫy đáp án tinh tế hơn. Thích hợp cho người học đã nắm vững nền tảng và muốn nâng cao tốc độ làm bài.`,sections:[{id:`listening`,skill:`listening`,title:`Listening`,durationMin:30,transcript:`A: I bought this kettle last week, and it stopped working yesterday.(B: I'm sorry about that. Do you have your receipt with you?(A: Yes, here it is. I'd rather have a refund, please.(B: Of course. The money will go back to the card you paid with.(A: I'd like to join the evening photography course. Is there still space?(B: We have two places left on Tuesday, but the Thursday course is full.(A: Tuesday is fine for me. How much does the course cost?(B: It's eighty pounds for eight weeks, including the darkroom sessions.(A: Hi Dan, the train from Bristol is forty minutes late.(B: Really? Shall we meet at the cafe instead of the station?(A: Good idea. I'll be there at half past six.(B: Perfect. I'll book a table near the window.(A: Excuse me, I think I left my umbrella on the chair by the door.(B: Let me check. Yes, a blue umbrella with a wooden handle?(A: That's it! Thank you so much.(B: We found it just after you left. It's behind the counter.(A: What time does breakfast start? We'd like an early start tomorrow.(B: Breakfast is served from six thirty, but hot food is only available from seven.(A: We'll come down at seven, then.(B: Very good. Your table is in the garden room.(Speaker: Good afternoon, everyone. I'm the manager of the Riverside Sports Centre.(Speaker: From next week, the swimming pool will close at nine instead of ten on weekdays.(Speaker: The gym and the two studios will keep their usual hours.(Speaker: Members can book classes up to seven days in advance, using the app or the front desk.(Speaker: Please note that the car park will be resurfaced during the first week of May.(Speaker: Until the work is finished, we ask you to leave your car at the leisure centre on King Street.(Speaker: Finally, our new family membership starts at twenty-five pounds a month.(Speaker: Last year I spent four months working on a small farm in Wales.(Speaker: I looked after the sheep, collected the eggs, and helped in the kitchen.(Speaker: In exchange, I received free accommodation and all my meals.(Speaker: The work started at seven every morning, so I went to bed early.(Speaker: At first, the hard work made me tired, but after two weeks I felt stronger than ever.(Speaker: The best part was the evening: the whole family cooked together and told stories.(Speaker: I also improved my English, because the family spoke very little Vietnamese.(Speaker: I would recommend this kind of experience to anyone who wants to learn how to live simply.`.split(`(`),questions:[{id:1,type:`multiple_choice`,question:`Part 1. Conversation 1. What does the customer want?`,options:[`A refund`,`A repair`,`A replacement kettle`,`A discount voucher`],answer:0,transcriptRef:2,explanationVi:`transcriptRef = 2: 'I'd rather have a refund, please' → đáp án A. B sai vì khách không yêu cầu sửa (máy hỏng sau một tuần); C sai vì khách không đổi sản phẩm; D không được nhắc.`},{id:2,type:`multiple_choice`,question:`Part 1. Conversation 2. How many places are left on the Tuesday photography course?`,options:[`One`,`Three`,`Two`,`Four`],answer:2,transcriptRef:5,explanationVi:`transcriptRef = 5: 'We have two places left on Tuesday' → đáp án C. Khóa thứ Năm đã kín (full) nên không còn chỗ; A và D không khớp con số nào trong hội thoại.`},{id:3,type:`multiple_choice`,question:`Part 1. Conversation 3. Where will the two friends meet?`,options:[`At the station`,`At the cafe`,`At home`,`At the office`],answer:1,transcriptRef:9,explanationVi:`transcriptRef = 9: 'Shall we meet at the cafe instead of the station?' → đáp án B. A là nơi ban đầu họ định gặp nhưng đã bị thay thế ('instead of'); C, D không được nhắc.`},{id:4,type:`multiple_choice`,question:`Part 1. Conversation 4. What colour is the lost umbrella?`,options:[`White`,`Black`,`Green`,`Blue`],answer:3,transcriptRef:13,explanationVi:`transcriptRef = 13: 'a blue umbrella with a wooden handle' → đáp án D. A, B, C đều là màu khác, không khớp mô tả của nhân viên.`},{id:5,type:`multiple_choice`,question:`Part 1. Conversation 5. When can the guests have hot food?`,options:[`Seven o'clock`,`Six thirty`,`Six o'clock`,`Half past seven`],answer:0,transcriptRef:17,explanationVi:`transcriptRef = 17: 'Breakfast is served from six thirty, but hot food is only available from seven' → đáp án A. B là giờ bắt đầu có đồ ăn nhẹ chứ không có đồ nóng; C và D không được nhắc.`},{id:6,type:`multiple_choice`,question:`Part 2. Talk 1. What is changing at the swimming pool?`,options:[`It will close one hour later on weekdays.`,`It will open earlier on weekdays.`,`It will close one hour earlier on weekdays.`,`It will close at the weekend.`],answer:2,transcriptRef:21,explanationVi:`transcriptRef = 21: 'the swimming pool will close at nine instead of ten on weekdays' → đóng lúc 9h thay vì 10h = sớm hơn 1 giờ → C đúng. A trái ngược; B nói về giờ mở cửa (không đổi); D không được nhắc.`},{id:7,type:`multiple_choice`,question:`Part 2. Talk 1. Where should members park while the car park is resurfaced?`,options:[`At the sports centre itself`,`At the leisure centre on King Street`,`On the newly resurfaced car park`,`In the garden room`],answer:1,transcriptRef:25,explanationVi:`transcriptRef = 25: 'leave your car at the leisure centre on King Street' → đáp án B. A là chỗ đang bị thi công nên không đỗ được; D là phòng ăn sáng của khách sạn trong hội thoại trước, hoàn toàn lạc đề.`},{id:8,type:`multiple_choice`,question:`Part 2. Talk 2. What did the speaker receive in exchange for her work?`,options:[`A small salary`,`Free transport`,`English lessons`,`Free accommodation and all meals`],answer:3,transcriptRef:29,explanationVi:`transcriptRef = 29: 'In exchange, I received free accommodation and all my meals' → đáp án D. A sai vì không có lương; B, C không được nhắc — cô học tiếng Anh nhờ trò chuyện với gia đình chứ không qua khóa học.`},{id:9,type:`multiple_choice`,question:`Part 2. Talk 2. Why did the speaker go to bed early?`,options:[`Because work started at seven in the morning.`,`Because there was no electricity on the farm.`,`Because she was ill.`,`Because the family slept at eight every night.`],answer:0,transcriptRef:30,explanationVi:`transcriptRef = 30: 'The work started at seven every morning, so I went to bed early' → đáp án A. B, C, D là các lý do không tồn tại trong đoạn; 'so' chỉ ra quan hệ nhân quả đúng.`},{id:10,type:`multiple_choice`,question:`Part 2. Talk 2. What was the best part of the experience for the speaker?`,options:[`Working with the sheep in the morning`,`Cooking and telling stories with the family in the evening`,`Receiving free accommodation`,`Learning to drive a tractor`],answer:1,transcriptRef:32,explanationVi:`transcriptRef = 32: 'The best part was the evening: the whole family cooked together and told stories' → đáp án B. A là công việc buổi sáng; C chỉ là điều kiện trao đổi; D không được nhắc tới.`}]},{id:`reading`,skill:`reading`,title:`Reading`,durationMin:30,paragraphs:[`Learning a musical instrument is more than a pleasant hobby. Researchers who studied children over five years found that those who practised an instrument regularly remembered spoken instructions better than those who did not. Playing also teaches patience, because progress is slow and visible only after months of practice. However, not every family can afford private lessons. Some schools have responded by offering group lessons at lunchtime, and several charities now lend musical instruments to pupils free of charge for a whole term.`,`A team of psychologists asked two groups of people to think of new uses for ordinary objects. One group sat in a chair, while the other walked at their own pace on a quiet path. On average, the walkers produced twice as many ideas, and their ideas were judged as more original by independent readers. Interestingly, the benefit continued for a short time after the walk had ended. The researchers warn, however, that busy roads and crowded pavements remove the advantage, because the brain has to focus on traffic instead of the task.`,`In 2015, the seaside town of Amberford charged ten pence for every plastic bag in its shops. Within a year, the number of bags found on the local beach had fallen by seventy percent. Cafe owners reported that fewer customers asked for take-away cups, and the market traders began selling cloth bags printed with the town's logo. The scheme was so successful that the council used the money raised to employ two extra street cleaners. Visitors now often mention the clean harbour in online reviews.`,`For many years, students were advised to type their lecture notes on a laptop. A recent experiment suggests that handwriting may be better for learning. Students who wrote by hand produced fewer words, but they understood the ideas behind those words more deeply, because they had to choose what to write while the lecture was still going on. Typists, by contrast, often tried to copy every sentence. The researchers do not argue that computers are harmful; they simply recommend that students review their typed notes by rewriting the key points in a notebook.`],questions:[{id:11,type:`multiple_choice`,question:`What did researchers find about children who practised an instrument regularly?`,options:[`They made more friends at school.`,`They played faster than other children.`,`They remembered spoken instructions better.`,`They needed less sleep at night.`],answer:2,paragraphRef:0,locationVi:`Đoạn 1, câu 'Researchers who studied children over five years found that those who practised an instrument regularly remembered spoken instructions better ...'`,explanationVi:`Câu thứ 2 của đoạn 1 nêu đúng kết quả 'remembered spoken instructions better' → C đúng. A, B, D không xuất hiện trong đoạn.`},{id:12,type:`multiple_choice`,question:`Why does playing an instrument teach patience, according to the passage?`,options:[`Because progress is slow and visible only after months of practice.`,`Because lessons are usually very expensive.`,`Because the teachers are strict.`,`Because practice must be done in a group.`],answer:0,paragraphRef:0,locationVi:`Đoạn 1, câu 'Playing also teaches patience, because progress is slow and visible only after months of practice.'`,explanationVi:`Câu 'because' giải thích nguyên nhân trực tiếp: tiến bộ chậm, chỉ thấy sau nhiều tháng tập → A đúng. B, C, D là các lý do không được nêu trong đoạn.`},{id:13,type:`true_false_not_given`,question:`Statement: Some families cannot afford private music lessons.`,options:[`True`,`False`,`Not Given`],answer:0,paragraphRef:0,locationVi:`Đoạn 1, câu 'However, not every family can afford private lessons.'`,explanationVi:`'Not every family can afford' nghĩa là có những gia đình không đủ tiền → Statement True. Đoạn không hề nói mọi gia đình đều có thể chi trả.`},{id:14,type:`gap_filling`,question:`Complete the sentence using NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage. Several charities now lend musical ___ to pupils free of charge for a whole term.`,answer:`instruments`,paragraphRef:0,locationVi:`Đoạn 1, câu cuối '... several charities now lend musical instruments to pupils free of charge ...'`,explanationVi:`Câu cuối đoạn 1 dùng đúng 'lend musical instruments to pupils' → điền 'instruments' (số nhiều theo 'musical ___ to pupils'). 'Guitars' hay 'books' không nằm trong câu gốc.`},{id:15,type:`multiple_choice`,question:`What is the main idea of the first paragraph?`,options:[`Children should stop taking private lessons.`,`Schools only teach music at lunchtime.`,`Researchers have proved that music is just a hobby.`,`Playing an instrument helps learning and character, but cost is a problem for some families.`],answer:3,paragraphRef:0,locationVi:`Đoạn 1 (toàn đoạn): 3 câu đầu nói về lợi ích, 2 câu cuối nói về rào cản chi phí.`,explanationVi:`Đoạn nêu lợi ích (trí nhớ, kiên nhẫn) rồi chuyển bằng 'However' sang rào cản chi phí → D đúng. A, B, C trái với tinh thần hoặc đưa ra tuyên bố không có trong đoạn.`},{id:16,type:`multiple_choice`,question:`What happened when one group of people walked while doing the task?`,options:[`They forgot the original task.`,`They produced twice as many ideas.`,`They walked faster than usual.`,`They preferred sitting down after the walk.`],answer:1,paragraphRef:1,locationVi:`Đoạn 2, câu 'On average, the walkers produced twice as many ideas ...'`,explanationVi:`Câu thứ 3 của đoạn 2 nêu 'walkers produced twice as many ideas' → B đúng. A, C, D không được đoạn văn nhắc tới.`},{id:17,type:`multiple_choice`,question:`What did the independent readers think of the ideas?`,options:[`The walkers' ideas were too short.`,`The seated group produced better ideas.`,`All the ideas were equally original.`,`The walkers' ideas were more original.`],answer:3,paragraphRef:1,locationVi:`Đoạn 2, câu '... their ideas were judged as more original by independent readers.'`,explanationVi:`Các độc giả độc lập đánh giá ý tưởng của nhóm đi bộ 'more original' → D đúng. B trái ngược với kết quả; A, C không được nêu.`},{id:18,type:`true_false_not_given`,question:`Statement: The creative benefit disappeared immediately after the walk ended.`,options:[`True`,`False`,`Not Given`],answer:1,paragraphRef:1,locationVi:`Đoạn 2, câu 'Interestingly, the benefit continued for a short time after the walk had ended.'`,explanationVi:`Đoạn nói lợi ích 'continued for a short time after the walk' → mâu thuẫn với 'disappeared immediately' → Statement False.`},{id:19,type:`gap_filling`,question:`Complete the sentence using NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage. Busy roads remove the advantage because the brain must focus on ___ instead of the task.`,answer:`traffic`,paragraphRef:1,locationVi:`Đoạn 2, câu cuối '... the brain has to focus on traffic instead of the task.'`,explanationVi:`Câu cuối đoạn 2 dùng đúng 'focus on traffic instead of the task' → điền 'traffic'. 'Roads' sai vì chủ ngữ đã là 'the brain'; các từ khác không có trong câu gốc.`},{id:20,type:`multiple_choice`,question:`What warning do the researchers give in the last sentence?`,options:[`Crowded, busy environments reduce the benefit of walking.`,`Walking is dangerous for the brain.`,`Psychologists prefer crowded pavements.`,`Traffic always improves creativity.`],answer:0,paragraphRef:1,locationVi:`Đoạn 2, câu cuối '... busy roads and crowded pavements remove the advantage ...'`,explanationVi:`Các nhà nghiên cứu cảnh báo đường ồn ào và vỉa hè đông đúc 'remove the advantage' → A đúng. D trái ngược; B và C diễn giải sai mục đích của cảnh báo.`},{id:21,type:`multiple_choice`,question:`How much did the town of Amberford charge for one plastic bag?`,options:[`Ten pounds`,`Seventy pence`,`Ten pence`,`One pence`],answer:2,paragraphRef:2,locationVi:`Đoạn 3, câu 'In 2015, the seaside town of Amberford charged ten pence for every plastic bag ...'`,explanationVi:`Đoạn 3 nêu rõ 'ten pence for every plastic bag' → C đúng. B là con số phần trăm giảm rác thải; A sai về đơn vị (pound thay vì pence); D không được nhắc.`},{id:22,type:`multiple_choice`,question:`What happened to the number of plastic bags on the local beach?`,options:[`It fell by seventy percent.`,`It rose by seventy percent.`,`It stayed exactly the same.`,`It was reduced by ten pence.`],answer:0,paragraphRef:2,locationVi:`Đoạn 3, câu 'Within a year, the number of bags found on the local beach had fallen by seventy percent.'`,explanationVi:`Câu thứ 2 của đoạn 3 dùng 'had fallen by seventy percent' → A đúng. B sai vì đảo nghĩa (fall ≠ rise); C trái với số liệu; D trộn lẫn đơn vị tiền với số lượng rác.`},{id:23,type:`multiple_choice`,question:`What did the market traders begin selling after the scheme started?`,options:[`Plastic bottles with the town's logo.`,`Take-away cups at a lower price.`,`Ten-pence harbour tickets.`,`Cloth bags printed with the town's logo.`],answer:3,paragraphRef:2,locationVi:`Đoạn 3, câu '... the market traders began selling cloth bags printed with the town's logo.'`,explanationVi:`Câu thứ 3 của đoạn 3 nêu thương nhân chợ bắt đầu bán 'cloth bags printed with the town's logo' → D đúng. A sai vì loại túi (vải, không phải nhựa); B, C không được nhắc.`},{id:24,type:`gap_filling`,question:`Complete the sentence using NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage. Within a year, the number of plastic bags on the beach had ___ by seventy percent.`,answer:`fallen`,paragraphRef:2,locationVi:`Đoạn 3, câu '... the number of bags found on the local beach had fallen by seventy percent.'`,explanationVi:`Câu gốc dùng 'had fallen by seventy percent' → điền 'fallen' (past participle sau 'had'). 'Fell' sai hình thức; 'reduced' không nằm trong câu gốc nên không đạt yêu cầu 'from the passage'.`},{id:25,type:`true_false_not_given`,question:`Statement: The council spent the money from the scheme on two extra street cleaners.`,options:[`True`,`False`,`Not Given`],answer:0,paragraphRef:2,locationVi:`Đoạn 3, câu '... the council used the money raised to employ two extra street cleaners.'`,explanationVi:`Nội dung câu này trùng khớp chính xác với câu trong đoạn 3 → Statement True. Không có thông tin nào mâu thuẫn.`},{id:26,type:`multiple_choice`,question:`What did students who wrote by hand do differently?`,options:[`They copied every sentence quickly.`,`They selected the most important points while listening.`,`They wrote twice as many words as the typists.`,`They finished the lecture before the teacher.`],answer:1,paragraphRef:3,locationVi:`Đoạn 4, câu '... they had to choose what to write while the lecture was still going on.'`,explanationVi:`Nhóm viết tay phải 'choose what to write' trong lúc nghe → họ chọn ý chính → B đúng. A mô tả nhóm gõ máy ('copy every sentence'); C sai vì nhóm viết tay viết 'fewer words'; D không được nhắc.`},{id:27,type:`multiple_choice`,question:`What do the researchers recommend?`,options:[`Stopping the use of laptops in class.`,`Typing only during the first half of a lecture.`,`Reviewing typed notes by rewriting the key points.`,`Writing every sentence by hand.`],answer:2,paragraphRef:3,locationVi:`Đoạn 4, câu cuối '... they simply recommend that students review their typed notes by rewriting the key points in a notebook.'`,explanationVi:`Lời khuyên cuối đoạn là 'review typed notes by rewriting the key points' → C đúng. A, D quá cực đoan (nghiên cứu 'không argument computers are harmful'); B không được nêu.`},{id:28,type:`true_false_not_given`,question:`Statement: The research team plans to repeat the experiment next year.`,options:[`True`,`False`,`Not Given`],answer:2,paragraphRef:3,locationVi:`Đoạn 4 (toàn đoạn) — không có câu nào đề cập tới kế hoạch lặp lại thí nghiệm.`,explanationVi:`Đoạn 4 chỉ mô tả kết quả và lời khuyên, không nói gì về kế hoạch làm lại thí nghiệm trong năm tới → Not Given (không đủ thông tin để kết luận).`},{id:29,type:`gap_filling`,question:`Complete the sentence using NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage. Typists often tried to copy every ___ during the lecture.`,answer:`sentence`,paragraphRef:3,locationVi:`Đoạn 4, câu 'Typists, by contrast, often tried to copy every sentence.'`,explanationVi:`Câu gốc là 'tried to copy every sentence' → điền 'sentence'. 'Word' hay 'idea' không nằm trong câu gốc nên sai yêu cầu 'from the passage'.`},{id:30,type:`multiple_choice`,question:`What is the main idea of the fourth paragraph?`,options:[`Handwriting may deepen understanding, and typed notes should be reviewed by rewriting key points.`,`Laptops should be banned from all lectures.`,`Typing is always better than writing by hand.`,`Students should write every word by hand.`],answer:0,paragraphRef:3,locationVi:`Đoạn 4 (toàn đoạn): kết quả thí nghiệm ở giữa và lời khuyên ở câu cuối.`,explanationVi:`Đoạn nêu viết tay giúp hiểu sâu hơn rồi kết thúc bằng lời khuyên gõ lại ý chính → A đúng. B, D quá cực đoan và trái với 'do not argue that computers are harmful'; C phủ nhận kết quả thí nghiệm.`}]},{id:`writing`,skill:`writing`,title:`Writing`,promptVi:`Viết một email ngắn (80–120 từ) cho người bạn nước ngoài tên Jack, mời cậu ấy đến thăm quê em vào dịp lễ gần nhất. Nêu ít nhất hai lý do nên đến và gợi ý hai hoạt động các em có thể làm cùng nhau.`,requirementsVi:[`Đúng số từ: 80–120 từ`,`Định dạng email: lời chào, nội dung, lời kết`,`Nêu ít nhất hai lý do nên đến thăm`,`Gợi ý ít nhất hai hoạt động cụ thể`,`Kết thúc bằng một câu hỏi hoặc lời mời phản hồi`],minWords:80,maxWords:120,sampleAnswer:`Dear Jack, How are you? I hope you are doing well. I am writing to invite you to visit my hometown during the national holiday next month. There are two good reasons to come: the weather is cool at this time of year, and the food festival in the old street lasts for a whole week. We could visit the night market together and try the local dishes, or we could rent bicycles and ride along the river. Please let me know if you can come, and I will book a room for you. Best wishes, Linh`},{id:`speaking`,skill:`speaking`,title:`Speaking`,promptVi:`Nói trong 2 phút về một địa điểm du lịch em rất muốn đến. Hãy nêu: địa điểm đó là đâu, em biết về nó như thế nào, em muốn làm gì ở đó, và vì sao em muốn đến.`,timeLimitSec:120,sampleAnswer:`The place I would really like to visit is the town of Hoi An in central Vietnam. I first saw it in a film two years ago, and I have wanted to go there ever since. What attracts me most is the old part of the town, where the houses are painted yellow and lanterns hang over every street. If I went there, I would walk along the river at night, take a boat under the lanterns, and learn to cook two or three local dishes in a short class. I would also like to take many photos of the narrow streets. I believe Hoi An is special because it is quiet and traditional, not crowded like a big city.`}]},{id:`exam-003`,code:`B1-003`,name:`Đề thi thử số 3`,type:`advanced`,level:`B1`,difficulty:`hard`,durationMin:60,description:`Đề thi thử số 3 mức nâng cao với từ vựng học thuật và các câu hỏi suy luận. Dành cho người học muốn thử thách bản thân trước kỳ thi thật.`,sections:[{id:`listening`,skill:`listening`,title:`Listening`,durationMin:30,transcript:`A: There's a mistake on my electricity bill — it's almost double last month's.(B: Let me check your account. I see that you submitted a meter reading on the first.(A: I did, but the bill seems to use an estimated reading instead.(B: You're right. I'll send it back for correction and you'll receive a revised bill within five working days.(A: I'm calling about the interview for the design assistant post.(B: Yes, we've moved it to Friday morning because two panel members are away.(A: Friday is difficult — I finish my shift at nine.(B: In that case, we can offer you the last slot at half past eleven.(A: The heating in my flat has stopped working again.(B: When did you first notice it?(A: Two days ago, but I thought it would fix itself overnight.(B: It won't. I'll send an engineer tomorrow afternoon, and please leave the keys with your neighbour.(A: I'd like to return these shoes I ordered online. They're the wrong size.(B: No problem. Do you have the dispatch note?(A: Yes, but I've worn them outside, so the soles are a bit dirty.(B: I'm afraid we can't accept them once they've been worn outside. You could exchange them for a different size instead.(A: My daughter has broken a front tooth and needs to see someone today.(B: The dentist is fully booked, but I can fit her in at four o'clock if it's urgent.(A: It is urgent — she's in pain.(B: Then come straight over. Please bring her with you and fill in the new-patient form.(Speaker: Before the fourteenth century, few people in Europe could tell the exact time.(Speaker: Monasteries kept the hours for prayer, but ordinary townspeople relied on the sun and the church bell.(Speaker: When public clock towers appeared in wealthy trading cities, the market day became strictly scheduled.(Speaker: Merchants could agree on an exact hour, so a late arrival was no longer a matter of opinion.(Speaker: Historians have argued that this shift helped create the habit of punctuality that we still expect today.(Speaker: The towers were also symbols of power: only cities that could afford craftsmen and bronze built them.(Speaker: My team has been restoring coral on the western reef for six years.(Speaker: We grow young corals in underwater nurseries until they are strong enough to move.(Speaker: The fragments are then fixed to the damaged rock using a special, marine-safe glue.(Speaker: Roughly seven out of ten transplanted fragments survive the first year.(Speaker: The greatest threats are not divers but warm water and the crown-of-thorns starfish.(Speaker: Visitors can help by choosing operators that follow the reef code and by not touching the coral.(Speaker: We now train local fishermen as technicians, because they know the reef better than anyone.`.split(`(`),questions:[{id:1,type:`multiple_choice`,question:`Part 1. Conversation 1. What is wrong with the electricity bill?`,options:[`It was sent to the wrong address.`,`The meter reading was submitted twice.`,`It was based on an estimated reading.`,`The price of electricity has doubled.`],answer:2,transcriptRef:2,explanationVi:`transcriptRef = 2: 'the bill seems to use an estimated reading instead' (thay vì số đọc thực tế khách đã gửi) → đáp án C. A, B, D không phải lỗi được mô tả; số liệu 'double' chỉ là mức độ chênh lệch, không phải nguyên nhân.`},{id:2,type:`multiple_choice`,question:`Part 1. Conversation 2. When will the interview take place?`,options:[`Friday morning`,`Friday at half past eleven`,`Thursday at half past eleven`,`Monday at nine o'clock`],answer:1,transcriptRef:7,explanationVi:`transcriptRef = 7: vì khách tan ca lúc 9 giờ, nhân viên đề xuất 'the last slot at half past eleven' vào thứ Sáu → đáp án B. A đúng ngày nhưng không đúng khung giờ; C, D là ngày hoặc giờ không có trong hội thoại.`},{id:3,type:`multiple_choice`,question:`Part 1. Conversation 3. What does the landlord ask the tenant to do?`,options:[`Repair the heating himself.`,`Wait for a phone call from the office.`,`Leave the flat for the whole afternoon.`,`Leave the keys with his neighbour.`],answer:3,transcriptRef:11,explanationVi:`transcriptRef = 11: 'please leave the keys with your neighbour' để kỹ thuật viên vào nhà → đáp án D. A sai vì khách không tự sửa; B, C không được nhắc — kỹ thuật viên sẽ đến vào chiều mai chứ không gọi trước.`},{id:4,type:`multiple_choice`,question:`Part 1. Conversation 4. What solution does the shop offer the customer?`,options:[`She can exchange the shoes for a different size.`,`She can get a full refund immediately.`,`She can wear the shoes inside and return them later.`,`She can ask the manufacturer for a repair.`],answer:0,transcriptRef:15,explanationVi:`transcriptRef = 15: hàng đã đi ra ngoài nên không nhận trả lại, nhưng 'You could exchange them for a different size instead' → đáp án A. B sai vì không hoàn tiền; C sai vì giày đã mang ra ngoài; D không được đề cập.`},{id:5,type:`multiple_choice`,question:`Part 1. Conversation 5. What is the mother advised to do?`,options:[`Come at four o'clock without her daughter.`,`Book an appointment for next week.`,`Come straight over with her daughter and fill in the form.`,`Wait until the dentist is free.`],answer:2,transcriptRef:19,explanationVi:`transcriptRef = 19: 'come straight over. Please bring her with you and fill in the new-patient form' → đáp án C. A sai vì bắt buộc đưa con theo; B sai vì ca khẩn cấp được nhận trong ngày; D trái với hướng dẫn của lễ tân.`},{id:6,type:`multiple_choice`,question:`Part 2. Talk 1. How did ordinary townspeople tell the time before clock towers?`,options:[`From public clock towers in the market.`,`From the sun and the church bell.`,`From small pocket watches.`,`From the market schedule.`],answer:1,transcriptRef:21,explanationVi:`transcriptRef = 21: 'ordinary townspeople relied on the sun and the church bell' → đáp án B. A và D là kết quả sau khi có đồng hồ tháp; C không tồn tại trước thế kỷ 14 (đoạn nói 'few people could tell the exact time').`},{id:7,type:`multiple_choice`,question:`Part 2. Talk 1. Why were clock towers symbols of power?`,options:[`Only wealthy cities could afford the craftsmen and bronze.`,`They told the exact time for free.`,`They were built by foreign kings.`,`They were taller than the churches.`],answer:0,transcriptRef:25,explanationVi:`transcriptRef = 25: 'only cities that could afford craftsmen and bronze built them' → chỉ thành phố giàu mới có → đáp án A. B, C, D là các chi tiết không có trong đoạn; đồng hồ tháp không miễn phí hay do vua nước ngoài xây.`},{id:8,type:`multiple_choice`,question:`Part 2. Talk 2. What happens to the coral fragments after they are strong enough?`,options:[`They are thrown back onto the reef.`,`They are tied to the rock with rope.`,`They are painted with a safe colour.`,`They are fixed to the damaged rock with special glue.`],answer:3,transcriptRef:28,explanationVi:`transcriptRef = 28: 'fixed to the damaged rock using a special, marine-safe glue' → đáp án D. A, B, C là các phương pháp không được nhắc; chi tiết 'glue' là mốc thông tin duy nhất đúng.`},{id:9,type:`multiple_choice`,question:`Part 2. Talk 2. What is the survival rate of transplanted coral in the first year?`,options:[`About three out of ten`,`About seven out of ten`,`About five out of ten`,`Almost all of it`],answer:1,transcriptRef:29,explanationVi:`transcriptRef = 29: 'Roughly seven out of ten transplanted fragments survive the first year' → đáp án B. A là phần còn lại (3/10); C và D không khớp số liệu nào trong đoạn.`},{id:10,type:`multiple_choice`,question:`Part 2. Talk 2. Who does the team now train as technicians?`,options:[`University students`,`Local divers`,`Local fishermen`,`Foreign engineers`],answer:2,transcriptRef:32,explanationVi:`transcriptRef = 32: 'We now train local fishermen as technicians, because they know the reef better than anyone' → đáp án C. A, B, D là các nhóm không được nhắc trong đoạn.`}]},{id:`reading`,skill:`reading`,title:`Reading`,durationMin:30,paragraphs:[`Students often revise a topic the night before a test and forget most of it a week later. Cognitive psychologists have shown that spacing the same amount of revision across several days produces much better long-term recall. In one study, participants learned four dozen foreign words. The group that reviewed the words after one day, one week, and one month remembered nearly twice as much as the group that crammed everything into a single session. The brain appears to strengthen a memory each time it is retrieved after a short period of forgetting.`,`A passive house uses up to ninety percent less energy for heating than an ordinary building, and it does so without expensive technology. The design is simple: very thick insulation, triple-glazed windows, and an airtight structure that keeps warm air inside. A small heat pump, powered by electricity, then supplies the rest. Critics point out that the construction cost is about fifteen percent higher, yet owners recover the difference within eight years through lower bills. Several European countries have now made similar standards compulsory for all new homes.`,`When the price of coffee fell sharply in 2001, thousands of small farmers in the highlands of Vien Lam were forced to sell their land. Those who survived often did so by changing the way they worked: instead of selling raw beans at the market, they began roasting and packing the coffee themselves. A cooperative formed in 2006 now exports directly to roasters in Europe, which cuts out three middlemen. The farmers also shade their coffee plants with native trees, which protects the soil and provides a home for birds.`,`On a hot afternoon, the centre of a large city can be five degrees warmer than the fields around it. Dark surfaces such as asphalt absorb sunlight during the day and release it slowly at night, while cars, air conditioners, and factories add even more heat. Trees offer a cheap defence: a mature tree can shade a pavement and release water vapour through its leaves, lowering the temperature beneath it. A study of twelve cities found that neighbourhoods with mature street trees reported fewer heat-related hospital visits. Planting is only the beginning, however, because young trees need several years of watering before they help.`],questions:[{id:11,type:`multiple_choice`,question:`In the study, which group remembered more of the foreign words?`,options:[`The group that crammed everything into one session.`,`The group that spaced its revision over days and weeks.`,`Both groups remembered exactly the same amount.`,`The group that learned only four words.`],answer:1,paragraphRef:0,locationVi:`Đoạn 1, câu 'The group that reviewed the words after one day, one week, and one month remembered nearly twice as much ...'`,explanationVi:`Nhóm ôn cách quãng (1 ngày, 1 tuần, 1 tháng) nhớ 'gần gấp đôi' → B đúng. A là nhóm nhớ ít hơn; C trái với 'nearly twice as much'; D sai số lượng (học bốn chục từ, không phải bốn từ).`},{id:12,type:`multiple_choice`,question:`What does the brain appear to do with a memory?`,options:[`Forget it completely after one week.`,`Store words faster than numbers.`,`Refuse to retrieve information at night.`,`Strengthen it each time it is retrieved after a period of forgetting.`],answer:3,paragraphRef:0,locationVi:`Đoạn 1, câu cuối 'The brain appears to strengthen a memory each time it is retrieved after a short period of forgetting.'`,explanationVi:`Câu cuối đoạn nêu đúng 'strengthen a memory each time it is retrieved after a short period of forgetting' → D đúng. A, B, C không được đoạn văn đề cập.`},{id:13,type:`true_false_not_given`,question:`Statement: The participants in the study learned four dozen foreign words.`,options:[`True`,`False`,`Not Given`],answer:0,paragraphRef:0,locationVi:`Đoạn 1, câu 'In one study, participants learned four dozen foreign words.'`,explanationVi:`Câu thứ 3 của đoạn 1 nêu đúng 'participants learned four dozen foreign words' → Statement True, không có thông tin mâu thuẫn.`},{id:14,type:`gap_filling`,question:`Complete the sentence using NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage. The spaced group remembered nearly twice as much as the group that ___ everything into a single session.`,answer:`crammed`,paragraphRef:0,locationVi:`Đoạn 1, câu '... as the group that crammed everything into a single session.'`,explanationVi:`Câu gốc dùng 'the group that crammed everything into a single session' → điền 'crammed'. 'Studied' hay 'put' không nằm trong câu gốc nên không đạt yêu cầu 'from the passage'.`},{id:15,type:`multiple_choice`,question:`What is the main idea of the first paragraph?`,options:[`Spacing revision over time leads to better long-term recall than cramming.`,`Foreign words are easier to learn than grammar.`,`Tests should be held only in the evening.`,`Psychologists advise revising only once before a test.`],answer:0,paragraphRef:0,locationVi:`Đoạn 1 (toàn đoạn): nguyên lý ở câu 2, thí nghiệm ở câu 3–4, cơ chế ở câu 5.`,explanationVi:`Đoạn khẳng định chia đều việc ôn tập cho kết quả nhớ lâu hơn ('spacing ... produces much better long-term recall') → A đúng. B, C là chủ đề không có; D ngược với thông điệp của đoạn.`},{id:16,type:`multiple_choice`,question:`How much less heating energy does a passive house use?`,options:[`Fifteen percent`,`Fifty percent`,`Up to ninety percent`,`Exactly eighty percent`],answer:2,paragraphRef:1,locationVi:`Đoạn 2, câu đầu 'A passive house uses up to ninety percent less energy for heating ...'`,explanationVi:`Câu mở đầu đoạn 2 nêu 'up to ninety percent less energy' → C đúng. A (15%) là phần chênh lệch chi phí xây dựng; B và D không xuất hiện trong đoạn.`},{id:17,type:`multiple_choice`,question:`What do critics of passive houses point out?`,options:[`The construction cost is about fifteen percent higher.`,`The houses look ugly.`,`Owners never recover the extra cost.`,`Triple-glazed windows are too cold.`],answer:0,paragraphRef:1,locationVi:`Đoạn 2, câu 'Critics point out that the construction cost is about fifteen percent higher ...'`,explanationVi:`Các nhà phê bình nêu 'construction cost is about fifteen percent higher' → A đúng. C sai vì chủ nhà hoàn lại khoản chênh trong tám năm (mệnh đề 'yet'); B, D không được nhắc.`},{id:18,type:`true_false_not_given`,question:`Statement: A passive house requires expensive technology to work.`,options:[`True`,`False`,`Not Given`],answer:1,paragraphRef:1,locationVi:`Đoạn 2, câu đầu '... and it does so without expensive technology.'`,explanationVi:`Đoạn nói rõ công nghệ không đắt đỏ ('without expensive technology') → Statement mâu thuẫn → False.`},{id:19,type:`gap_filling`,question:`Complete the sentence using NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage. The structure of a passive house is ___, which keeps the warm air inside.`,answer:`airtight`,paragraphRef:1,locationVi:`Đoạn 2, câu '... and an airtight structure that keeps warm air inside.'`,explanationVi:`Câu gốc là 'an airtight structure that keeps warm air inside'; cấu trúc 'is ___' cần tính từ → 'airtight'. 'Warm' hay 'thick' sai nghĩa hoặc nằm ở vị trí khác trong câu gốc.`},{id:20,type:`multiple_choice`,question:`What is the main advantage of the design described in the second paragraph?`,options:[`It requires no electricity at all.`,`It achieves large energy savings with a simple design.`,`It costs less to build than an ordinary house.`,`It uses thick windows to store heat.`],answer:1,paragraphRef:1,locationVi:`Đoạn 2, câu 1–2: 'ninety percent less energy' + 'The design is simple ...'`,explanationVi:`Đoạn nêu tiết kiệm tới 90% năng lượng trong khi 'design is simple' → B đúng. C sai vì chi phí xây cao hơn 15%; A sai vì vẫn dùng nhiệt bơm nóng chạy bằng điện; D hiểu sai chức năng của cửa ba lớp.`},{id:21,type:`multiple_choice`,question:`What happened to thousands of coffee farmers after the price fell in 2001?`,options:[`They were forced to sell their land.`,`They moved to the capital city.`,`They formed a cooperative that same year.`,`They started planting native trees immediately.`],answer:0,paragraphRef:2,locationVi:`Đoạn 3, câu '... thousands of small farmers in the highlands of Vien Lam were forced to sell their land.'`,explanationVi:`Câu đầu đoạn 3 nêu 'were forced to sell their land' → A đúng. C sai vì hợp tác xã thành lập năm 2006, không phải 2001; B, D không được nhắc.`},{id:22,type:`multiple_choice`,question:`What does the cooperative do differently?`,options:[`It sells raw beans at the local market.`,`It buys land from the middlemen.`,`It stops growing coffee and trades instead.`,`It exports directly to roasters in Europe.`],answer:3,paragraphRef:2,locationVi:`Đoạn 3, câu 'A cooperative formed in 2006 now exports directly to roasters in Europe, which cuts out three middlemen.'`,explanationVi:`Hợp tác xã 'exports directly to roasters in Europe' → D đúng. A là cách làm cũ mà họ đã bỏ; B, C trái với nội dung đoạn (vẫn trồng cà phê, không mua đất).`},{id:23,type:`true_false_not_given`,question:`Statement: The farmers now sell raw beans directly to roasters in Europe.`,options:[`True`,`False`,`Not Given`],answer:1,paragraphRef:2,locationVi:`Đoạn 3, câu '... instead of selling raw beans at the market, they began roasting and packing the coffee themselves.'`,explanationVi:`Họ không bán hạt thô (raw beans) nữa mà tự rang và đóng gói rồi xuất khẩu → Statement mâu thuẫn với đoạn → False.`},{id:24,type:`gap_filling`,question:`Complete the sentence using NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage. Instead of selling raw beans at the market, the farmers began ___ and packing the coffee themselves.`,answer:`roasting`,paragraphRef:2,locationVi:`Đoạn 3, câu '... they began roasting and packing the coffee themselves.'`,explanationVi:`Câu gốc là 'began roasting and packing' → cần dạng V-ing sau 'began' → 'roasting'. 'Roast' (nguyên dạng) sai ngữ pháp; 'growing' không nằm trong câu gốc.`},{id:25,type:`multiple_choice`,question:`What do the coffee farmers do that helps the local environment?`,options:[`They irrigate the plants with river water.`,`They grow coffee under native trees.`,`They sell birds to local zoos.`,`They remove all trees from the hillsides.`],answer:1,paragraphRef:2,locationVi:`Đoạn 3, câu cuối 'The farmers also shade their coffee plants with native trees, which protects the soil and provides a home for birds.'`,explanationVi:`Câu cuối nêu họ che bóng cà phê bằng cây bản địa, bảo vệ đất và làm tổ cho chim → B đúng. D trái ngược (giữ cây, không chặt); A, C không được nhắc.`},{id:26,type:`multiple_choice`,question:`Why can the centre of a large city be hotter than the fields around it?`,options:[`Because the fields around it are always cooler.`,`Because young trees drink all the available water.`,`Because dark surfaces absorb and release heat, and machines add more.`,`Because it rains less often in the centre.`],answer:2,paragraphRef:3,locationVi:`Đoạn 4, câu 'Dark surfaces such as asphalt absorb sunlight during the day and release it slowly at night, while cars, air conditioners, and factories add even more heat.'`,explanationVi:`Câu thứ 2 của đoạn 4 nêu hai nguyên nhân: bề mặt tối hấp thụ/giải nhiệt và máy móc tạo thêm nhiệt → C đúng. A chỉ nói vòng vo; B, D không có trong đoạn.`},{id:27,type:`multiple_choice`,question:`How does a mature tree cool the pavement beneath it?`,options:[`By shading it and releasing water vapour through its leaves.`,`By covering the pavement with dark asphalt.`,`By running air conditioners underneath.`,`By reflecting the lights of nearby hospitals.`],answer:0,paragraphRef:3,locationVi:`Đoạn 4, câu '... a mature tree can shade a pavement and release water vapour through its leaves, lowering the temperature beneath it.'`,explanationVi:`Cây che bóng ('shade') và thoát hơi nước ('release water vapour') → hạ nhiệt bên dưới → A đúng. B làm tăng nhiệt (bề mặt tối); C, D không liên quan đến cây.`},{id:28,type:`true_false_not_given`,question:`Statement: The research team plans to repeat the study in twelve more cities.`,options:[`True`,`False`,`Not Given`],answer:2,paragraphRef:3,locationVi:`Đoạn 4, câu 'A study of twelve cities found ...' — không có câu nào về kế hoạch nghiên cứu tiếp theo.`,explanationVi:`Đoạn chỉ nói nghiên cứu diễn ra ở mười hai thành phố, không nói gì về việc lặp lại ở mười hai thành phố khác → Not Given (thiếu thông tin).`},{id:29,type:`gap_filling`,question:`Complete the sentence using NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the passage. Neighbourhoods with mature street trees reported fewer heat-related hospital ___ .`,answer:`visits`,paragraphRef:3,locationVi:`Đoạn 4, câu '... reported fewer heat-related hospital visits.'`,explanationVi:`Câu gốc là 'fewer heat-related hospital visits'; sau 'fewer' cần danh từ số nhiều → 'visits'. 'Visit' (số ít) sai ngữ pháp với 'fewer'; 'patients' không nằm trong câu gốc.`},{id:30,type:`multiple_choice`,question:`What warning does the last sentence give?`,options:[`Trees cannot survive in city centres.`,`Hospital visits will rise again soon.`,`Asphalt is cheaper than planting trees.`,`Planting trees takes years of care before it has an effect.`],answer:3,paragraphRef:3,locationVi:`Đoạn 4, câu cuối 'Planting is only the beginning, however, because young trees need several years of watering before they help.'`,explanationVi:`'Planting is only the beginning' + cây non cần nhiều năm tưới nước 'before they help' → trồng không phải xong ngay → D đúng. A, B, C không được đoạn văn khẳng định.`}]},{id:`writing`,skill:`writing`,title:`Writing`,promptVi:`Viết một đoạn văn (80–120 từ) nêu quan điểm của em về ý kiến: 'Các thành phố nên chi nhiều tiền hơn để trồng cây xanh trên đường phố.' Đưa ra ít nhất hai lý do và một ví dụ hoặc số liệu minh họa.`,requirementsVi:[`Đúng số từ: 80–120 từ`,`Nêu rõ quan điểm ở phần mở đầu`,`Đưa ít nhất hai lý do để ủng hộ quan điểm`,`Kèm một ví dụ hoặc số liệu minh họa cụ thể`,`Có câu kết luận tóm lại quan điểm`],minWords:80,maxWords:120,sampleAnswer:`In my opinion, cities should spend more money on planting street trees. First, trees lower the temperature in hot city centres. Studies show that neighbourhoods with mature trees are cooler and report fewer heat-related hospital visits. Second, trees clean the air and give people shade, so residents can walk or cycle more comfortably. For example, in my district, a row of new trees along the main road has made the walk to school much more pleasant in summer. Planting trees costs money and takes years of care, but the long-term benefits for health are worth it.`},{id:`speaking`,skill:`speaking`,title:`Speaking`,promptVi:`Nói trong 2 phút về cách em ghi nhớ kiến thức hiệu quả nhất khi ôn tập. Hãy nêu: em thường ôn theo cách nào, vì sao cách đó hiệu quả với em, và em khuyên bạn bè nên tránh thói quen ôn tập nào.`,timeLimitSec:120,sampleAnswer:`The way I remember things best is to spread my revision over several days instead of studying everything the night before an exam. For example, when I learn new English words, I review them the next day, then again after a week, and once more after a month. Each time I try to recall the words before I look at the answers, and that effort makes the memory stronger. Research shows that this method can help you remember nearly twice as much as cramming. I always advise my friends to avoid reading their notes again and again in one long session, because it feels easy but the knowledge disappears quickly.`}]},{id:`exam-004`,code:`B1-004`,name:`Đề tổng hợp số 4`,type:`comprehensive`,level:`B1`,difficulty:`hard`,durationMin:60,description:`Đề tổng hợp bốn kỹ năng theo format VSTEP bậc 3: Listening 10 câu (5 hội thoại ngắn + 1 đoạn nói), Reading 20 câu trên 4 đoạn văn (trắc nghiệm, True/False/Not Given, điền từ), Writing dạng đoạn nghị luận và Speaking với bài mẫu. Dành cho người học muốn luyện toàn diện trong 60 phút.`,sections:[{id:`listening`,skill:`listening`,title:`Listening`,durationMin:30,transcript:`Part 1. Questions 1 to 5. You will hear five short conversations. Choose the correct answer for each question.(Conversation 1. A man phones a community college about an evening course.(M: Hello, I'd like to sign up for the evening photography course.(W: Certainly. The Tuesday group is full, but we still have places on Wednesday at seven.(M: Wednesday is fine. Does the fee include the camera equipment?(W: No, you need to bring your own camera. The price of ninety pounds covers all the handouts.(Conversation 2. A woman returns a kettle to a shop.(W: I bought this kettle last week and it stopped working yesterday.(M: I'm sorry about that. Would you like a replacement or a full refund?(W: A refund, please. I would rather choose a different model myself.(M: Certainly. The money will go back to your card within three working days.(Conversation 3. Two friends arrange a game of tennis.(M: Are you still free to play tennis on Saturday morning?(W: The courts are booked until eleven, so let's meet at half past eleven instead.(M: Great. Shall I bring the balls this time?(W: Yes, please. I still owe you from last month.(Conversation 4. A man asks about a lost phone.(W: Lost property office. How can I help you?(M: I left my phone in a taxi on Friday night. It has a blue cover.(W: We had one handed in this morning. It was found on the back seat of a black cab.(M: That must be mine. What time can I collect it?(W: Any time after ten tomorrow morning.(Conversation 5. A woman books a table at a restaurant.(M: Good evening, Bellini's restaurant.(W: I would like a table for four this Friday at eight, please.(M: We are fully booked at eight, but I can offer you nine fifteen.(W: That is a little late. What about half past seven?(M: Seven thirty is fine. Could you give me your phone number?(Part 2. Questions 6 to 10. You will hear a talk about a city library.(You will hear a librarian explaining the changes at Westfield Library.(Good morning. My name is Helen Morris, and I am the head librarian at Westfield Library.(From Monday, the library will open at nine in the morning instead of ten.(The evening hours stay the same, so we still close at eight on weekdays.(The ground floor has been redesigned. The children's corner now sits next to the café.(You can borrow up to twenty books at a time instead of twelve.(The loan period has also been extended from two weeks to three weeks.(Late books now cost ten pence a day, and the first late day is always free.(Our free computer class for beginners starts on 3 June and lasts six weeks.(Places are limited, so please sign up at the front desk.(Thank you for listening, and I am happy to answer any questions.`.split(`(`),questions:[{id:1,type:`multiple_choice`,question:`What does the man need to bring to the photography course?`,options:[`A camera`,`A textbook`,`A laptop`,`A tripod`],answer:0,transcriptRef:5,explanationVi:`Dòng 5 nói “you need to bring your own camera” → anh ấy phải tự mang máy ảnh. Sách giáo khoa, laptop và chân máy không được nhắc tới trong hội thoại.`},{id:2,type:`multiple_choice`,question:`What does the woman decide to do about the kettle?`,options:[`Have it repaired`,`Get her money back`,`Wait for a new model`,`Exchange it for a toaster`],answer:1,transcriptRef:9,explanationVi:`Dòng 9: “A refund, please” → cô ấy muốn nhận lại tiền (lựa chọn 2). Cô ấy không chọn cách sửa hay đổi máy mới (A, C) và cũng không đổi lấy máy nướng (D).`},{id:3,type:`multiple_choice`,question:`When will the two friends play tennis?`,options:[`At nine on Saturday morning`,`At eleven on Saturday morning`,`At half past eleven on Saturday morning`,`At half past seven on Saturday morning`],answer:2,transcriptRef:13,explanationVi:`Dòng 13: sân đặt đến 11 giờ nên họ hẹn “at half past eleven” (11 giờ rưỡi sáng thứ Bảy). 9 giờ, 11 giờ tròn và 7 giờ rưỡi đều không khớp.`},{id:4,type:`multiple_choice`,question:`Where was the man's phone found?`,options:[`In a restaurant`,`In a cinema`,`In a taxi`,`In the man's office`],answer:2,transcriptRef:19,explanationVi:`Dòng 19: điện thoại “found on the back seat of a black cab” → trong taxi. Nhà hàng, rạp chiếu phim và văn phòng không xuất hiện ở cuộc hội thoại này.`},{id:5,type:`multiple_choice`,question:`What time will the woman's table be booked for?`,options:[`Half past seven`,`Eight o'clock`,`Nine fifteen`,`Half past nine`],answer:0,transcriptRef:27,explanationVi:`Dòng 27 xác nhận “Seven thirty is fine” (7 giờ rưỡi). 8 giờ đã kín (dòng 25), còn 9 giờ 15 chỉ là phương án ban đầu bị cô ấy từ chối.`},{id:6,type:`multiple_choice`,question:`What time will Westfield Library open on weekday mornings from Monday?`,options:[`At eight`,`At nine`,`At ten`,`At eleven`],answer:1,transcriptRef:31,explanationVi:`Dòng 31: “open at nine in the morning instead of ten” → đổi từ 10 giờ sang 9 giờ. 8 và 11 giờ không được nhắc đến.`},{id:7,type:`multiple_choice`,question:`Where is the children's corner now?`,options:[`On the first floor`,`Next to the café`,`Opposite the entrance`,`Beside the car park`],answer:1,transcriptRef:33,explanationVi:`Dòng 33: “The children's corner now sits next to the café” → cạnh quán cà phê. Tầng lầu, lối vào và bãi đỗ xe không có trong đoạn.`},{id:8,type:`multiple_choice`,question:`How many books can members borrow at one time now?`,options:[`Twelve`,`Fifteen`,`Twenty`,`Twenty-five`],answer:2,transcriptRef:34,explanationVi:`Dòng 34: “up to twenty books ... instead of twelve” → tối đa 20 cuốn (12 là quy định cũ). 15 và 25 không được nêu.`},{id:9,type:`multiple_choice`,question:`How long is the loan period now?`,options:[`One week`,`Two weeks`,`Three weeks`,`Four weeks`],answer:2,transcriptRef:35,explanationVi:`Dòng 35: “extended from two weeks to three weeks” → kéo dài từ hai lên ba tuần; một tuần và bốn tuần đều sai.`},{id:10,type:`multiple_choice`,question:`What must people do to join the free computer class?`,options:[`Call the librarian`,`Send an email`,`Pay a small fee`,`Sign up at the front desk`],answer:3,transcriptRef:38,explanationVi:`Dòng 38: “please sign up at the front desk” → đăng ký trực tiếp tại quầy (lựa chọn 4). Lớp miễn phí nên không có phí (sai lựa chọn 3); gọi điện hay gửi email không được nhắc.`}]},{id:`reading`,skill:`reading`,title:`Reading`,durationMin:30,paragraphs:[`In many cities, unused pieces of land are being turned into community gardens. A community garden is a single piece of land that a group of people, usually those living nearby, garden together. Families are given small plots where they grow vegetables, herbs and flowers for their own use. Some gardens also sell their produce at a small market to raise money for tools and seeds. The movement began in the 1970s, when city residents in North America started reclaiming empty lots, and it has spread quickly to Europe and Asia over the last decade. Today, a single city may have more than fifty gardens.`,`The benefits go far beyond fresh food. Studies from two universities in the Netherlands found that people who garden regularly sleep better and feel less stressed. Working with soil also gives neighbours a reason to talk to each other, which reduces loneliness, especially among older residents. Children who take part learn where their food comes from and are more willing to eat vegetables. Because fruit and vegetables travel only a few metres instead of hundreds, community gardens also cut pollution from transport. Some cities even use the gardens to teach school classes outdoors.`,`However, running a garden is not easy. Plots have to be watered even during holidays, and volunteers often struggle with pests without using strong chemicals. Gardens in poor areas may lack tools, soil and clean water. There is also the problem of land tenure: councils sometimes sell the land to developers and give the gardeners only a short notice. In one survey, a third of the gardens closed within five years, most often because the land was needed for building. Volunteers often spend their own money on repairs as well.`,`Despite these problems, the future looks promising. Many cities now include community gardens in their long-term plans and give them cheap, long leases. Schools use the gardens for science lessons, and several hospitals prescribe garden time for patients recovering from stress. Experts believe that as cities grow warmer and food prices rise, more residents will want to grow at least some of their own food. The humble community garden, they argue, is becoming an important part of city life.`],questions:[{id:1,type:`multiple_choice`,question:`What is a community garden?`,options:[`A garden for children only`,`A piece of land gardened together by a group of people`,`A garden behind a supermarket`,`A place where farmers sell machines`],answer:1,paragraphRef:0,locationVi:`Đoạn 1, câu “A community garden is a single piece of land that a group of people ... garden together.”`,explanationVi:`Đoạn 1 định nghĩa rõ vườn cộng đồng là mảnh đất một nhóm người cùng trồng trọt → đúng lựa chọn 2. Lựa chọn 1 sai vì không chỉ dành cho trẻ em; 3 và 4 hoàn toàn không có trong đoạn.`},{id:2,type:`multiple_choice`,question:`Why do some community gardens sell their produce at a small market?`,options:[`To raise money`,`To feed their members`,`To pay the council tax`,`To import new seeds`],answer:0,paragraphRef:0,locationVi:`Đoạn 1, câu “Some gardens also sell their produce at a small market to raise money for tools and seeds.”`,explanationVi:`Đoạn 1 nói bán để “raise money for tools and seeds” → gây quỹ. Nuôi thành viên, trả thuế hội đồng và nhập hạt giống không phải mục đích nêu ra.`},{id:3,type:`multiple_choice`,question:`When and where did the community garden movement begin?`,options:[`In the 1950s in Europe`,`In the 1990s in Asia`,`In the 1970s in North America`,`Ten years ago in Australia`],answer:2,paragraphRef:0,locationVi:`Đoạn 1, câu “The movement began in the 1970s, when city residents in North America started reclaiming empty lots ...”`,explanationVi:`Đoạn 1 nêu “began in the 1970s ... North America” → đúng lựa chọn 3. Các mốc 1950s, 1990s và “mười năm trước” đều không khớp.`},{id:4,type:`multiple_choice`,question:`What did the Dutch studies find about people who garden regularly?`,options:[`They earn more money`,`They sleep better and feel less stressed`,`They move to the countryside`,`They eat more meat`],answer:1,paragraphRef:1,locationVi:`Đoạn 2, câu “Studies from two universities in the Netherlands found that people who garden regularly sleep better and feel less stressed.”`,explanationVi:`Đoạn 2 nói người trồng vườn “sleep better and feel less stressed” → đúng lựa chọn 2. Thu nhập, nơi ở và thói quen ăn thịt không được nghiên cứu nào nhắc tới.`},{id:5,type:`multiple_choice`,question:`Why can community gardens reduce loneliness?`,options:[`Because neighbours have a reason to talk to each other`,`Because the gardens are near schools`,`Because gardening costs nothing`,`Because older residents all live together`],answer:0,paragraphRef:1,locationVi:`Đoạn 2, câu “Working with soil also gives neighbours a reason to talk to each other, which reduces loneliness ...”`,explanationVi:`Đoạn 2 nêu nguyên nhân trực tiếp là hàng xóm “have a reason to talk to each other” → đúng lựa chọn 1. Ba lý do còn lại không xuất hiện trong đoạn.`},{id:6,type:`multiple_choice`,question:`What do children who take part in a community garden learn?`,options:[`How to cook large meals`,`How to sell food online`,`Which tools are expensive`,`Where their food comes from`],answer:3,paragraphRef:1,locationVi:`Đoạn 2, câu “Children who take part learn where their food comes from and are more willing to eat vegetables.”`,explanationVi:`Đoạn 2: trẻ “learn where their food comes from” → đúng lựa chọn 4. Nấu ăn số lượng lớn, bán online và giá dụng cụ không được nêu.`},{id:7,type:`multiple_choice`,question:`Why can community gardens cut pollution from transport?`,options:[`Because gardeners walk to work`,`Because the land is near the motorway`,`Because fruit and vegetables travel only a few metres`,`Because the produce is frozen`],answer:2,paragraphRef:1,locationVi:`Đoạn 2, câu “Because fruit and vegetables travel only a few metres instead of hundreds, community gardens also cut pollution from transport.”`,explanationVi:`Đoạn 2 giải thích nhờ quãng đường vận chuyển chỉ vài mét → đúng lựa chọn 3. Đi bộ, gần đường cao tốc và đông lạnh đều không phải lý do trong bài.`},{id:8,type:`multiple_choice`,question:`What do volunteers have to do even during holidays?`,options:[`Sell the vegetables`,`Water the plots`,`Meet the council`,`Buy chemicals`],answer:1,paragraphRef:2,locationVi:`Đoạn 3, câu “Plots have to be watered even during holidays ...”`,explanationVi:`Đoạn 3: “Plots have to be watered even during holidays” → phải tưới trong kỳ nghỉ → đúng lựa chọn 2. Bán rau, gặp hội đồng và mua hóa chất không gắn với “holidays”.`},{id:9,type:`multiple_choice`,question:`What is the problem of land tenure mentioned in the text?`,options:[`Councils may sell the land and give the gardeners short notice`,`The plots are too small for families`,`Gardeners must pay high taxes on the land`,`The soil on the land is not fertile`],answer:0,paragraphRef:2,locationVi:`Đoạn 3, câu “councils sometimes sell the land to developers and give the gardeners only a short notice.”`,explanationVi:`Đoạn 3 giải thích land tenure là việc đất có thể bị bán cho nhà phát triển và người trồng chỉ được báo trước ngắn → đúng lựa chọn 1. Ba ý còn lại không có trong đoạn.`},{id:10,type:`multiple_choice`,question:`Why did a third of the community gardens close within five years?`,options:[`There was too much rain`,`Vegetables became cheaper`,`The land was needed for building`,`Volunteers moved abroad`],answer:2,paragraphRef:2,locationVi:`Đoạn 3, câu “a third of the gardens closed within five years, most often because the land was needed for building.”`,explanationVi:`Đoạn 3 nêu nguyên nhân trực tiếp: “the land was needed for building” → đúng lựa chọn 3. Mưa nhiều, rau rẻ và tình nguyện viên chuyển đi không được nhắc.`},{id:11,type:`multiple_choice`,question:`What do many cities now offer community gardens?`,options:[`Free electricity`,`New gardening tools`,`Bigger families`,`Cheap, long leases`],answer:3,paragraphRef:3,locationVi:`Đoạn 4, câu “Many cities now include community gardens in their long-term plans and give them cheap, long leases.”`,explanationVi:`Đoạn 4: các thành phố cho vườn “cheap, long leases” (hợp đồng thuê dài hạn, giá rẻ) → đúng lựa chọn 4. Điện, dụng cụ và gia đình không thuộc chính sách này.`},{id:12,type:`multiple_choice`,question:`For whom do some hospitals prescribe garden time?`,options:[`Patients recovering from stress`,`Students before exams`,`Tourists visiting the city`,`Gardeners with injuries`],answer:1,paragraphRef:3,locationVi:`Đoạn 4, câu “several hospitals prescribe garden time for patients recovering from stress.”`,explanationVi:`Đoạn 4: bệnh viện chỉ định “for patients recovering from stress” → đúng lựa chọn 2. Học sinh, du khách và người trồng vườn bị thương không được nêu.`},{id:13,type:`true_false_not_given`,question:`The community garden movement began in North America.`,options:[`True`,`False`,`Not Given`],answer:0,paragraphRef:0,locationVi:`Đoạn 1, câu “The movement began in the 1970s, when city residents in North America started reclaiming empty lots ...”`,explanationVi:`Đoạn 1 nói rõ nơi khởi đầu là Bắc Mỹ → đúng (True). Không có thông tin nào mâu thuẫn, nên không chọn False hay Not Given.`},{id:14,type:`true_false_not_given`,question:`The Dutch studies focused on children who garden.`,options:[`True`,`False`,`Not Given`],answer:2,paragraphRef:1,locationVi:`Đoạn 2 — đoạn chỉ nói kết quả nghiên cứu về “people who garden”, không nêu đối tượng là trẻ em.`,explanationVi:`Đoạn 2 không nói trẻ em có phải đối tượng nghiên cứu hay không → Not Given. Bài không xác nhận (không phải True) và cũng không phủ nhận (không phải False).`},{id:15,type:`true_false_not_given`,question:`Volunteers find it easy to control pests without using strong chemicals.`,options:[`True`,`False`,`Not Given`],answer:1,paragraphRef:2,locationVi:`Đoạn 3, câu “volunteers often struggle with pests without using strong chemicals.”`,explanationVi:`Đoạn 3 dùng “struggle with pests” (gặp khó khăn) → mâu thuẫn với “find it easy” → sai (False).`},{id:16,type:`true_false_not_given`,question:`Schools use community gardens for science lessons.`,options:[`True`,`False`,`Not Given`],answer:0,paragraphRef:3,locationVi:`Đoạn 4, câu “Schools use the gardens for science lessons ...”`,explanationVi:`Đoạn 4 nêu thẳng “Schools use the gardens for science lessons” → đúng (True); không có ý nào phủ nhận nên không chọn False hay Not Given.`},{id:17,type:`gap_filling`,question:`The movement began in the 1970s, when city residents started reclaiming empty ______.`,answer:`lots`,paragraphRef:0,locationVi:`Đoạn 1, câu “... started reclaiming empty lots ...”`,explanationVi:`Câu trong bài là “started reclaiming empty lots” → từ cần điền là “lots” (mảnh đất bỏ hoang). Các từ khác không khớp ngữ cảnh “empty ...”.`},{id:18,type:`gap_filling`,question:`Working with soil gives neighbours a reason to ______ to each other.`,answer:`talk`,paragraphRef:1,locationVi:`Đoạn 2, câu “Working with soil also gives neighbours a reason to talk to each other ...”`,explanationVi:`Đoạn 2 viết “a reason to talk to each other” → điền “talk”. “Speak to each other” cũng gần nghĩa nhưng đáp án đúng theo bài là “talk”.`},{id:19,type:`gap_filling`,question:`In one survey, a third of the gardens closed within five ______.`,answer:`years`,paragraphRef:2,locationVi:`Đoạn 3, câu “a third of the gardens closed within five years ...”`,explanationVi:`Đoạn 3 nêu “within five years” → điền “years”. “Months” hay “seasons” không được bài nhắc tới.`},{id:20,type:`gap_filling`,question:`Many cities now give community gardens cheap, long ______.`,answer:`leases`,paragraphRef:3,locationVi:`Đoạn 4, câu “... give them cheap, long leases.”`,explanationVi:`Đoạn 4 dùng “cheap, long leases” (hợp đồng thuê đất) → điền “leases”. “Loans”, “lands”, “areas” không đúng ngữ cảnh chính sách của thành phố.`}]},{id:`writing`,skill:`writing`,title:`Writing`,promptVi:`Nhiều thành phố đang biến những mảnh đất bỏ hoang trong khu dân cư thành vườn cộng đồng (community garden). Hãy viết một đoạn văn ngắn (80–120 từ) nêu quan điểm của bạn về việc người dân nên trồng rau trong vườn cộng đồng thay vì mua toàn bộ thực phẩm ở siêu thị.`,requirementsVi:[`Nêu rõ quan điểm ở câu đầu (nên hay không nên) và chốt lại quan điểm ở câu cuối.`,`Dùng ít nhất 2 lý do có ví dụ (ví dụ: sức khỏe, môi trường, quan hệ hàng xóm).`,`Liên kết ý bằng từ nối: firstly, in addition, however, overall…`,`Đúng 80–120 từ, sử dụng thì hiện tại và hiện tại tiếp diễn, chính tả chuẩn.`],minWords:80,maxWords:120,sampleAnswer:`In my opinion, city residents should grow vegetables in a community garden whenever it is possible. First of all, the food is fresher and healthier because it travels only a few metres instead of hundreds. In addition, a garden gives neighbours a reason to talk to each other, which makes a neighbourhood friendlier and less lonely. Children also learn where their food comes from and become more willing to eat vegetables. Of course, gardening takes time, and plots must be watered even on holidays. However, I believe the benefits are much greater than the work. Overall, community gardens are good for our health, our streets and our planet.`},{id:`speaking`,skill:`speaking`,title:`Speaking`,promptVi:`Nói trong 2 phút về một nơi công cộng ở thành phố bạn (công viên, thư viện, vườn cộng đồng…) mà bạn thường đến. Hãy nêu: (1) đó là đâu và bạn đi vào lúc nào; (2) bạn thường làm gì ở đó; (3) vì sao nơi đó quan trọng với bạn và mọi người xung quanh.`,timeLimitSec:120,sampleAnswer:`The place I want to talk about is Green Park, a public park near my house. I usually go there twice a week, on Sunday morning with my younger brother. We walk along the path, feed the birds and sometimes read under a big tree. What I like most is that the park is free and everyone can use it: children play football, old people do exercises and teenagers sit and talk. It matters to our community because it gives us a safe place to meet each other and to relax after a hard week. Without the park, my neighbourhood would feel much less friendly.`}]},{id:`exam-005`,code:`B1-005`,name:`Đề thi thử số 5`,type:`mock`,level:`B1`,difficulty:`medium`,durationMin:60,description:`Đề thi thử mô phỏng kỳ thi VSTEP bậc 3: Listening 10 câu (5 hội thoại + 1 thông báo), Reading 20 câu trên 4 đoạn văn với 4 dạng câu hỏi, Writing dạng email không chính thức và Speaking kèm bài mẫu. Dùng để kiểm tra trình độ trước kỳ thi thật trong 60 phút.`,sections:[{id:`listening`,skill:`listening`,title:`Listening`,durationMin:30,transcript:`Part 1. Questions 1 to 5. You will hear five short conversations. Choose the correct answer for each question.(Conversation 1. A woman asks for directions at Central Station.(W: Excuse me, which platform does the train to Oxford leave from?(M: Platform four today. It usually leaves from platform six, but there is engineering work.(W: And how long does the journey take?(M: About an hour and five minutes if you take the direct train.(Conversation 2. A man changes his dentist appointment.(W: Good morning, Dental Care Clinic.(M: Hello. I have an appointment at two on Thursday, but I cannot come.(W: We can move it to Friday at ten, or to Monday at four.(M: Friday morning suits me. Could we make it ten fifteen?(W: Ten fifteen is free. See you then.(Conversation 3. Two colleagues book a meeting room.(M: We need a room for the training session. How many people are coming?(W: Twelve, but three of them will join online.(M: Room two is big enough, and it has a screen for video calls.(W: Perfect. Is it free at two o'clock?(M: It is taken until three, so let's start at half past three.(Conversation 4. A woman buys a second-hand bike.(W: Is the blue bike still for sale?(M: Yes. I bought it two years ago for three hundred pounds, but I will take two hundred now.(W: The tyres look worn. Would you take one hundred and fifty?(M: One hundred and eighty, and I will include a new lock.(W: Deal.(Conversation 5. A man reserves a hotel room.(M: Hello, I would like a single room for the night of twelve June.(W: We have a room with a view of the garden for ninety pounds, or a quieter room at the back for seventy-five.(M: I am a light sleeper, so I will take the quiet room at the back for seventy-five pounds, please.(W: Certainly. Breakfast is served from seven until ten.(Part 2. Questions 6 to 10. You will hear an announcement about a sports centre.(You will hear a manager talking to the members of Riverside Sports Centre.(Good afternoon, everyone. From one September, Riverside Sports Centre will have longer opening hours.(We will open at six in the morning instead of seven, and close at eleven instead of ten at night.(The swimming pool will be closed for repairs from the third to the tenth of September.(During that week, members can use the pool at our North Road centre free of charge.(The new fitness room on the first floor has twelve more machines.(To avoid queues, please book badminton courts online; the old paper diary has been removed.(Classes continue as usual, except that yoga moves from Monday to Wednesday at six.(Finally, membership fees will rise by five pounds a month from October.(Existing members who pay for the whole year in advance will keep the old price.(If you have any questions, please speak to me or to my colleague Sam at reception.`.split(`(`),questions:[{id:1,type:`multiple_choice`,question:`Why does the train to Oxford leave from platform four today?`,options:[`The train is delayed`,`Platform six is closed for cleaning`,`There is engineering work`,`The train is longer than usual`],answer:2,transcriptRef:3,explanationVi:`Dòng 3: “It usually leaves from platform six, but there is engineering work” → có công trình sửa chữa. Chậm chuyến, dọn dẹp và chiều dài tàu không được nói tới.`},{id:2,type:`multiple_choice`,question:`When is the man's new dentist appointment?`,options:[`Friday at ten`,`Monday at four`,`Thursday at two`,`Friday at ten fifteen`],answer:3,transcriptRef:11,explanationVi:`Dòng 11 xác nhận “Ten fifteen is free. See you then.” → thứ Sáu lúc 10 giờ 15. Các mốc khác (thứ Hai 4 giờ, thứ Năm 2 giờ, thứ Sáu 10 giờ) đều là phương án cũ hoặc không được chốt.`},{id:3,type:`multiple_choice`,question:`When will the training session start?`,options:[`At half past three`,`At two o'clock`,`At three o'clock`,`At four o'clock`],answer:0,transcriptRef:17,explanationVi:`Dòng 17: phòng “is taken until three, so let's start at half past three” → bắt đầu 15 giờ 30. Hai giờ và ba giờ là giờ phòng còn bận.`},{id:4,type:`multiple_choice`,question:`What is the final price of the second-hand bike, including the lock?`,options:[`One hundred and fifty pounds`,`One hundred and eighty pounds`,`Two hundred pounds`,`Three hundred pounds`],answer:1,transcriptRef:22,explanationVi:`Dòng 22: “One hundred and eighty, and I will include a new lock” → chốt 180 bảng kèm khóa. 150 là mức người mua đề nghị, 200 và 300 là giá ban đầu.`},{id:5,type:`multiple_choice`,question:`How much will the man pay for his hotel room?`,options:[`Ninety pounds`,`Eighty pounds`,`Seventy-five pounds`,`Seventy pounds`],answer:2,transcriptRef:27,explanationVi:`Dòng 27: anh ấy chọn “the quiet room at the back”, giá 75 bảng (dòng 26). 90 bảng là phòng có view vườn mà anh ấy không chọn.`},{id:6,type:`multiple_choice`,question:`From 1 September, what time will Riverside Sports Centre open in the morning?`,options:[`Seven in the morning`,`Six in the morning`,`Eight in the morning`,`Ten at night`],answer:1,transcriptRef:32,explanationVi:`Dòng 32: “open at six in the morning instead of seven” → đổi sang 6 giờ sáng. 7 giờ là giờ cũ, 8 giờ và 10 giờ đêm không đúng.`},{id:7,type:`multiple_choice`,question:`Why will the swimming pool be closed?`,options:[`For a swimming competition`,`For cleaning`,`For the holidays`,`For repairs`],answer:3,transcriptRef:33,explanationVi:`Dòng 33: “closed for repairs from the third to the tenth of September” → sửa chữa. Không có giải đấu, việc dọn dẹp hay kỳ nghỉ nào được nhắc.`},{id:8,type:`multiple_choice`,question:`What can members do at the North Road centre during that week?`,options:[`Book badminton courts`,`Take yoga classes`,`Use the pool free of charge`,`Buy new machines`],answer:2,transcriptRef:34,explanationVi:`Dòng 34: “members can use the pool at our North Road centre free of charge” → bơi miễn phí ở North Road. Đặt sân, lớp yoga và mua máy không thuộc ưu đãi này.`},{id:9,type:`multiple_choice`,question:`How should members reserve a badminton court now?`,options:[`By calling reception`,`By booking online`,`By signing the paper diary`,`By coming in person`],answer:1,transcriptRef:36,explanationVi:`Dòng 36: “please book badminton courts online; the old paper diary has been removed” → đặt trực tuyến. Sổ giấy đã bỏ, gọi điện và đến tận nơi không được nêu.`},{id:10,type:`multiple_choice`,question:`What has changed about the yoga class?`,options:[`It has been cancelled`,`It has moved to the first floor`,`It is now two hours long`,`It is now on Wednesday at six`],answer:3,transcriptRef:37,explanationVi:`Dòng 37: “yoga moves from Monday to Wednesday at six” → đổi sang thứ Tư lúc 6 giờ. Lớp không bị hủy, không đổi tầng và không nói kéo dài.`}]},{id:`reading`,skill:`reading`,title:`Reading`,durationMin:30,paragraphs:[`Learning a musical instrument is one of the most popular hobbies among young people, and research suggests that its benefits go far beyond music. A study of two hundred children in London followed pupils who had a weekly violin lesson for a year. At the end of that year, the children were better at reading aloud and at telling small differences in sounds apart than pupils who had no musical training. Scientists believe this happens because playing music exercises the same parts of the brain that we use when we speak and read. Reading music also trains the ears to hear rhythm and pitch.`,`Music also teaches patience. Progress is slow at first: a beginner may need several weeks to play a simple tune without stopping. Students who continue for at least two years usually say that they learned how to break a difficult task into small steps and practise them one by one. Group lessons add another skill — listening to other players and keeping a steady beat together. These habits are useful outside music, in subjects such as mathematics and even in team sports, where timing matters.`,`Of course, there are difficulties. Lessons can be expensive, and a good instrument costs money too, so some families rent a piano instead of buying one. Practising every day can become boring, and many children give up in the first two years. Teachers say the answer is short, regular practice: fifteen minutes a day works better than two hours on Sunday. Parents can help by letting children choose the music they play and by going to their concerts instead of forcing them to practise every evening.`,`It is never too late to start. Adults who begin in their thirties or forties often progress faster than children at first, because they can already read music and manage their own practice time. Community centres now run evening classes for beginners, and many people take up the guitar after retirement to stay mentally active. Researchers found that older adults who played an instrument twice a week remembered words and names better than those who did no musical activity. Whatever your age, the first step is simply to pick up an instrument and try.`],questions:[{id:1,type:`multiple_choice`,question:`What did the London study find about the children who had violin lessons?`,options:[`They played football better`,`They were better at reading aloud`,`They needed less sleep`,`They were better at painting`],answer:1,paragraphRef:0,locationVi:`Đoạn 1, câu “the children were better at reading aloud and at telling small differences in sounds apart ...”`,explanationVi:`Đoạn 1 nêu rõ nhóm học vĩ cầm “better at reading aloud” → đúng lựa chọn 2. Bóng đá, giấc ngủ và hội họa không được so sánh trong nghiên cứu.`},{id:2,type:`multiple_choice`,question:`Why are pupils with musical training better at telling small differences in sounds apart?`,options:[`Because they practise more hours a day`,`Because they have private tutors`,`Because they listen to recordings every day`,`Because playing music exercises brain areas used for language`],answer:3,paragraphRef:0,locationVi:`Đoạn 1, câu “Scientists believe this happens because playing music exercises the same parts of the brain that we use when we speak and read.”`,explanationVi:`Đoạn 1 giải thích nhờ âm nhạc kích thích “the same parts of the brain that we use when we speak and read” → đúng lựa chọn 4. Thời gian tập, gia sư và nghe băng không phải nguyên nhân bài nêu.`},{id:3,type:`multiple_choice`,question:`What may a beginner need several weeks to do?`,options:[`Write an original song`,`Read music perfectly`,`Play a simple tune without stopping`,`Perform at a concert`],answer:2,paragraphRef:1,locationVi:`Đoạn 2, câu “a beginner may need several weeks to play a simple tune without stopping.”`,explanationVi:`Đoạn 2 viết “several weeks to play a simple tune without stopping” → đúng lựa chọn 3. Sáng tác, đọc nốt trọn vẹn và biểu diễn không được nhắc ở đây.`},{id:4,type:`multiple_choice`,question:`Students who continue for at least two years usually learn how to ______.`,options:[`Break a difficult task into small steps`,`Compose music for other people`,`Earn money from music`,`Teach younger children`],answer:0,paragraphRef:1,locationVi:`Đoạn 2, câu “they learned how to break a difficult task into small steps and practise them one by one.”`,explanationVi:`Đoạn 2: các em học được cách “break a difficult task into small steps” → đúng lựa chọn 1. Soạn nhạc, kiếm tiền và dạy trẻ nhỏ không xuất hiện.`},{id:5,type:`multiple_choice`,question:`What extra skill do group lessons add?`,options:[`Reading music faster`,`Playing without any mistakes`,`Memorising long pieces`,`Listening to other players and keeping a steady beat`],answer:3,paragraphRef:1,locationVi:`Đoạn 2, câu “Group lessons add another skill — listening to other players and keeping a steady beat together.”`,explanationVi:`Đoạn 2 nêu rõ kỹ năng thêm vào là “listening to other players and keeping a steady beat together” → đúng lựa chọn 4. Ba lựa chọn còn lại không được bài nói tới.`},{id:6,type:`multiple_choice`,question:`According to the second paragraph, where else are the habits learned in music useful?`,options:[`Only in music lessons`,`In art and drama only`,`In mathematics and team sports`,`Nowhere outside music`],answer:2,paragraphRef:1,locationVi:`Đoạn 2, câu “These habits are useful outside music, in subjects such as mathematics and even in team sports ...”`,explanationVi:`Đoạn 2 nêu “outside music ... mathematics and even in team sports” → đúng lựa chọn 3; các ý “chỉ trong nhạc”, “chỉ ở nghệ thuật” và “không có ích nơi khác” đều trái bài.`},{id:7,type:`multiple_choice`,question:`Why do some families rent a piano instead of buying one?`,options:[`Because pianos are too big for small flats`,`Because renting sounds better`,`Because a good instrument costs a lot`,`Because they move house every year`],answer:2,paragraphRef:2,locationVi:`Đoạn 3, câu “Lessons can be expensive, and a good instrument costs money too, so some families rent a piano ...”`,explanationVi:`Đoạn 3 nêu chi phí: “a good instrument costs money too” → mua đàn đắt nên thuê → đúng lựa chọn 3. Diện tích nhà, chất lượng âm thanh và việc chuyển nhà không phải lý do.`},{id:8,type:`multiple_choice`,question:`What do teachers recommend for practice?`,options:[`Two hours on Sunday`,`Practising only in the holidays`,`Two hours every day`,`Fifteen minutes every day`],answer:3,paragraphRef:2,locationVi:`Đoạn 3, câu “fifteen minutes a day works better than two hours on Sunday.”`,explanationVi:`Đoạn 3 so sánh trực tiếp: “fifteen minutes a day works better than two hours on Sunday” → đúng lựa chọn 4; hai giờ vào Chủ nhật hay trong kỳ nghỉ đều bị bài xếp kém hơn.`},{id:9,type:`multiple_choice`,question:`How can parents help children keep practising?`,options:[`Pay for every lesson`,`Practise the instrument with them every day`,`Choose the instrument for them`,`Let children choose their music and go to their concerts`],answer:3,paragraphRef:2,locationVi:`Đoạn 3, câu “Parents can help by letting children choose the music they play and by going to their concerts ...”`,explanationVi:`Đoạn 3 nêu hai cách: “letting children choose the music ... and going to their concerts” → đúng lựa chọn 4. Trả tiền, tập cùng mỗi ngày hay chọn đàn giùm không được khuyến nghị.`},{id:10,type:`multiple_choice`,question:`Why do adults often progress faster than children at the beginning?`,options:[`They have more free time`,`They can read music and manage their practice time`,`They buy more expensive instruments`,`They have younger teachers`],answer:1,paragraphRef:3,locationVi:`Đoạn 4, câu “Adults ... often progress faster than children at first, because they can already read music and manage their own practice time.”`,explanationVi:`Đoạn 4 nêu lý do “because they can already read music and manage their own practice time” → đúng lựa chọn 2. Thời gian rảnh, đàn đắt và thầy trẻ không được nói tới.`},{id:11,type:`multiple_choice`,question:`What did researchers find about older adults who played an instrument twice a week?`,options:[`They walked faster`,`They remembered words and names better`,`They slept longer`,`They heard sounds more clearly`],answer:1,paragraphRef:3,locationVi:`Đoạn 4, câu “older adults who played an instrument twice a week remembered words and names better ...”`,explanationVi:`Đoạn 4: nhóm này “remembered words and names better” → đúng lựa chọn 2. Chạy nhanh, ngủ lâu và thính giác không thuộc kết quả nghiên cứu.`},{id:12,type:`multiple_choice`,question:`What does the writer suggest as the first step for anyone who wants to learn?`,options:[`Wait until retirement`,`Buy the most expensive instrument`,`Take a year of theory first`,`Simply pick up an instrument and try`],answer:3,paragraphRef:3,locationVi:`Đoạn 4, câu “Whatever your age, the first step is simply to pick up an instrument and try.”`,explanationVi:`Câu kết: “the first step is simply to pick up an instrument and try” → đúng lựa chọn 4; chờ về hưu, mua đàn đắt hay học lý thuyết một năm đều trái ý tác giả.`},{id:13,type:`true_false_not_given`,question:`Pupils without musical training were better at telling small differences in sounds apart.`,options:[`True`,`False`,`Not Given`],answer:1,paragraphRef:0,locationVi:`Đoạn 1, câu “the children were better at ... telling small differences in sounds apart than pupils who had no musical training.”`,explanationVi:`Bài nói nhóm học vĩ cầm nghe tốt hơn nhóm không học → câu trên đảo ngược mối so sánh nên sai (False).`},{id:14,type:`true_false_not_given`,question:`A private charity paid for the London study.`,options:[`True`,`False`,`Not Given`],answer:2,paragraphRef:0,locationVi:`Đoạn 1 — đoạn chỉ mô tả cách nghiên cứu và kết quả, không nói gì về nguồn tài trợ.`,explanationVi:`Không có thông tin nào về người tài trợ cho nghiên cứu → Not Given; bài không xác nhận cũng không phủ nhận, nên không chọn True hay False.`},{id:15,type:`true_false_not_given`,question:`Many children stop learning an instrument within their first two years.`,options:[`True`,`False`,`Not Given`],answer:0,paragraphRef:2,locationVi:`Đoạn 3, câu “many children give up in the first two years.”`,explanationVi:`Đoạn 3 nêu “many children give up in the first two years” → trùng nghĩa với “stop learning ... within their first two years” → đúng (True).`},{id:16,type:`true_false_not_given`,question:`Community centres charge less for evening classes than private teachers do.`,options:[`True`,`False`,`Not Given`],answer:2,paragraphRef:3,locationVi:`Đoạn 4 — đoạn nói trung tâm tổ chức lớp buổi tối cho người mới bắt đầu, không so sánh học phí với giáo viên riêng.`,explanationVi:`Đoạn 4 không nêu mức học phí nào → không có căn cứ kết luận → Not Given; không có số liệu nào để xác nhận (True) hay phủ nhận (False).`},{id:17,type:`gap_filling`,question:`The London study followed two hundred ______ who had a weekly violin lesson.`,answer:`children`,paragraphRef:0,locationVi:`Đoạn 1, câu “A study of two hundred children in London followed pupils who had a weekly violin lesson ...”`,explanationVi:`Đoạn 1 viết “two hundred children in London” → điền “children”. “Pupils” cũng đúng ngữ nghĩa nhưng câu trong bài dùng “children”.`},{id:18,type:`gap_filling`,question:`In group lessons, students learn to listen to other players and keep a steady ______ together.`,answer:`beat`,paragraphRef:1,locationVi:`Đoạn 2, câu “listening to other players and keeping a steady beat together.”`,explanationVi:`Đoạn 2 dùng “keeping a steady beat together” (giữ nhịp) → điền “beat”. “Speed”, “rhythm section” không khớp cấu trúc “steady ...”.`},{id:19,type:`gap_filling`,question:`Practising every day can become ______, so many children give up in the first two years.`,answer:`boring`,paragraphRef:2,locationVi:`Đoạn 3, câu “Practising every day can become boring, and many children give up ...”`,explanationVi:`Đoạn 3 nêu “Practising every day can become boring” → điền “boring”. “Difficult”, “expensive” không đúng với ý nghĩa nêu trong câu này.`},{id:20,type:`gap_filling`,question:`Many people take up the guitar after ______ to stay mentally active.`,answer:`retirement`,paragraphRef:3,locationVi:`Đoạn 4, câu “many people take up the guitar after retirement to stay mentally active.”`,explanationVi:`Đoạn 4 viết “after retirement” → điền “retirement”. “School”, “work” hay “illness” không xuất hiện trong đoạn này.`}]},{id:`writing`,skill:`writing`,title:`Writing`,promptVi:`Bạn vừa nhận được hai vé tham dự lễ hội âm nhạc Starlight Music Festival vào cuối tuần này. Hãy viết email không chính thức (80–120 từ) cho người bạn thân tên Tom để: (1) báo tin và cho biết địa điểm, giờ bắt đầu; (2) mời Tom đi cùng và nêu lý do; (3) hỏi xem Tom có thể đến lúc mấy giờ và nên mang theo gì.`,requirementsVi:[`Đúng dạng email không chính thức: lời chào thân mật (Hi Tom), kết thúc bằng Bye/Best, giọng tự nhiên.`,`Trả lời đủ cả 3 ý trong đề bài, dùng thì hiện tại và thì tương lai (will / be going to).`,`Liên kết ý bằng từ nối: so, because, and then, by the way…`,`Đúng 80–120 từ, chính tả và dấu câu chuẩn.`],minWords:80,maxWords:120,sampleAnswer:`Hi Tom,

Guess what! I have just got two tickets for the Starlight Music Festival this Saturday, and it starts at two o'clock in Riverside Park. Would you like to come with me? I know you love rock bands, and a famous local group will play at six. We could meet at the main gate at half past one and have lunch there first. By the way, what time can you arrive? And do you think we should bring water and a blanket? The weather report says it will be sunny all day. Let me know tonight!

Bye,
Mai`},{id:`speaking`,skill:`speaking`,title:`Speaking`,promptVi:`Nói trong 2 phút về một chuyến đi (journey) mà bạn nhớ nhất. Hãy nêu: (1) bạn đã đi đâu, đi cùng ai và bằng phương tiện gì; (2) điều gì đã xảy ra trong chuyến đi; (3) vì sao chuyến đi đó để lại ấn tượng với bạn.`,timeLimitSec:120,sampleAnswer:`I would like to describe a journey that I still remember clearly. Two years ago, my cousin and I travelled to a small mountain town by night bus. The journey took eight hours, and the road was very winding, so we arrived early in the morning feeling tired but excited. When the sun rose, we saw rice fields and mist everywhere, which was the most beautiful view I had ever seen. We stayed for two days, walked to a waterfall and tried the local food. I remember this trip because it was my first journey without my parents, and it made me feel more independent.`}]}];export{e as t};